{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book","id":1055797,"title":"Thoughts on future werewolf 5ed by looking at the BNS book","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-02-27T14:42:15-08:00","id":1055797,"title":"Thoughts on future werewolf 5ed by looking at the BNS book","content":"<u><b>NOTE: This is not meant to be a hate piece or an attack on the future </b></u><u><b>WtA</b></u><u><b> content by White Wolf. It is to discuss and analyze it. It is also meant to showcase why some things it has would ill-fit </b></u><u><b>WtA</b></u><u><b> as currently stands.</b></u><br /> <br /> <br /> First of all, to not be unfair of the content, I'll start with the positives first;<br /> <br /> - The history section is not badly written and uses the content pretty well.<br /> <br /> -The splitting of the Nation has potential, if done right. I like that Shadow Lords headline the more tolerant faction, as well.<br /> <br /> -The Derangement rules are better and avoid fishmalky stuff.<br /> <br /> However, I have to be honest about the things that worry me;<br /> <br /> The Bitten: Yes, the 'bitten kinfolk turn to garou' has been kept.<br /> <br /> Furies and Males: In the history section, Furies suddenly start having male and female children equally and this makes them want to keep the male garou children. I have said this before and I say it again, the Furies shouldn't have to add males to the tribe. Their duty is to womanhood, and one has to respect sacred feminity a bit. Plus, it is like human Red Talons, going against the core ideals of the tribe.<br /> <br /> Glass Walkers and the Weaver: Glass Walkers are now happy for more Weaver things and being 'of the Wyld' is a negative thing to them. Glass Walkers, at least how I read the revised tb, knew Weaver was dangerous and tried to somehow help Gaia live in the cities. And yes, Wyld was a factor in that.<br /> <br /> Jobs: Yes, they are still listed with the auspices. Even to the Sanctum of Gaia tribes, for some reason.<br /> <br /> The thicker Gauntlet+fewer Caerns: Given how much the Nation was on its last legs with the Caerns and Gauntlet, this really does not feel like a good addition. While splitting of the Nation is a big thing, this entirely changes the core of the game. I'm not even bothered by the post-Apocalypse plot, but in general it takes away the feeling of keeping hold of what still remains and juggling between tradition and new ideas.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T14:47:40-08:00","id":1055798,"title":"","content":"i'v'e still knew to wta, could you tell me what's a bns and hw can i get the information you are mentioning here?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T14:49:54-08:00","id":1055801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nicolas Milioni</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1055798#post1055798\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">i'v'e still knew to wta, could you tell me what's a bns and hw can i get the information you are mentioning here?</div> </div> </div> </div>By NIght studios, the new LARP publisher for White Wolf. For -current- WtA content, I'd say go for Werewolf the Apocalypse 20th edition. If you want to check the book I mentioned here out, look for Minds Eye Theatre Werewolf the Apocalypse.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T14:56:55-08:00","id":1055807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1055801#post1055801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> By NIght studios, the new LARP publisher for White Wolf. For -current- WtA content, I'd say go for Werewolf the Apocalypse 20th edition. If you want to check the book I mentioned here out, look for Minds Eye Theatre Werewolf the Apocalypse.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! about the changes, i can see the GW'S being more resistant to the Wyld. See, the setting is there is a Apocalypse coming and that the Garou are going to lose everything, right? So it makes sense that they'd want to stick to what they know","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4621-nicolas-milioni","name":"Nicolas Milioni","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4621_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T14:57:45-08:00","id":1055808,"title":"","content":"Note: Glasswalker is my favorite tribe.<br /> <br /> I kind of hate how Glasswalkers are all &quot;Weaver good/Wyld bad.&quot; While I believe that is how the rest of the Garou nation sees Glasswalkers, I feel they see Weaver as a Tool and something to be controlled, rather than a preference over the Wyld.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T15:29:34-08:00","id":1055833,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar110_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"110\" data-vbnamecard=\"110\">Ana Mizuki</a>, thanks for the post. Now I'm a <i>more</i> apprehensive about the possible upcoming edition. I never paid attention to the BNS books. Why did the Garou Nation split? And who ended up where?<br /> <br /> Agreeing with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar3950_2.gif');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"3950\" data-vbnamecard=\"3950\">wonderandawe</a>, I don't like that take on the Glasswalkers. That really was just supposed to be how the other Garou viewed them. Not how they actually are.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T15:39:23-08:00","id":1055836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1055833#post1055833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar110_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"110\" data-vbnamecard=\"110\">Ana Mizuki</a>, thanks for the post. Now I'm a <i>more</i> apprehensive about the possible upcoming edition. I never paid attention to the BNS books. Why did the Garou Nation split? And who ended up where?<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Basically, the Nation split on whether they should follow the old ways and fight the Weaver while others wanted to allow new allies (vampires, fera and mages) and use the Weaver to fight the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> The split was;<br /> <br /> Sanctum of Gaia: Black Furies, Fianna, Get of Fenris, Red Talons, Silver Fangs and Wendigo<br /> <br /> Concordiat of the Stars: Bone Gnawers, Glass Walkers, Children of Gaia, Shadow Lords, Stargazers and Uktena<br /> <br /> Striders are neutral.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T15:56:59-08:00","id":1055842,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1055836#post1055836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Basically, the Nation split on whether they should follow the old ways and fight the Weaver while others wanted to allow new allies (vampires, fera and mages) and use the Weaver to fight the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> The split was;<br /> <br /> Sanctum of Gaia: Black Furies, Fianna, Get of Fenris, Red Talons, Silver Fangs and Wendigo<br /> <br /> Concordiat of the Stars: Bone Gnawers, Glass Walkers, Children of Gaia, Shadow Lords, Stargazers and Uktena<br /> <br /> Striders are neutral.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why the fuck would the Stargazers want to use the Weaver to fight the Wyrm? Or the Uktena, or any of them? They all have front-row seats for the Weaver's shit-show, 24/7, and the Stargazers are the main proponents outside of the Furies and Talons that say that the Weaver is possibly the real enemy! This split makes as much sense as the 2e Lunar factions!.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T16:00:48-08:00","id":1055845,"title":"","content":"I'm surprised that no one has made mention of the eighth sign of the phoenix...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","name":"Gangrel44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T16:02:33-08:00","id":1055847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1055842#post1055842\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Why the fuck would the Stargazers want to use the Weaver to fight the Wyrm? Or the Uktena, or any of them? They all have front-row seats for the Weaver's shit-show, 24/7, and the Stargazers are the main proponents outside of the Furies and Talons that say that the Weaver is possibly the real enemy! This split makes as much sense as the 2e Lunar factions!.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it is a split between allowing tribes vs traditional ones. I think MOST in the Star gang are there because Fera are allowed in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T16:05:48-08:00","id":1055852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1055836#post1055836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Basically, the Nation split on whether they should follow the old ways and fight the Weaver while others wanted to allow new allies (vampires, fera and mages) and use the Weaver to fight the Wyrm.<br /> <br /> The split was;<br /> <br /> Sanctum of Gaia: Black Furies, Fianna, Get of Fenris, Red Talons, Silver Fangs and Wendigo<br /> <br /> Concordiat of the Stars: Bone Gnawers, Glass Walkers, Children of Gaia, Shadow Lords, Stargazers and Uktena<br /> <br /> Striders are neutral.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds...terrible. I don't understand at all how the Tribes would have ended up that way.<br /> <br /> Should I even ask about the other Fera?<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gangrel44</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1055845#post1055845\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm surprised that no one has made mention of the eighth sign of the phoenix...</div> </div> </div> </div>... So what's going on with the eighth sign?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T16:11:18-08:00","id":1055854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book#post1055797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Jobs: Yes, they are still listed with the auspices. Even to the Sanctum of Gaia tribes, for some reason.</div> </div> </div> </div>What do you mean by jobs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T16:27:49-08:00","id":1055861,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1055854#post1055854\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What do you mean by jobs?</div> </div> </div> </div>As in, each tribe's auspice lists what jobs they would do in the human world. Bear in mind that this includes ahroun and galliards.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T16:42:38-08:00","id":1055869,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book#post1055797\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><u><b>NOTE: This is not meant to be a hate piece or an attack on the future </b></u><u><b>WtA</b></u><u><b> content by White Wolf. It is to discuss and analyze it. It is also meant to showcase why some things it has would ill-fit </b></u><u><b>WtA</b></u><u><b> as currently stands.</b></u><br /> <br /> The Bitten: Yes, the 'bitten kinfolk turn to garou' has been kept.<br /> <br /> Furies and Males: In the history section, Furies suddenly start having male and female children equally and this makes them want to keep the male garou children. I have said this before and I say it again, the Furies shouldn't have to add males to the tribe. Their duty is to womanhood, and one has to respect sacred feminity a bit. Plus, it is like human Red Talons, going against the core ideals of the tribe.<br /> <br /> Jobs: Yes, they are still listed with the auspices. Even to the Sanctum of Gaia tribes, for some reason.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Curious about the Bitten and Jobs, and wondering if you could give a few more details?<br /> <br /> As for the Furies, there was never a Birth disparity. They utilized strong relationships with other tribes to maintain numbers and 'balance'. Male Garou went to CoG, sometimes other tribes. They took in a disproportionate number of female lost cubs and occasional other converts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T16:51:20-08:00","id":1055874,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1055869#post1055869\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Curious about the Bitten and Jobs, and wondering if you could give a few more details?<br /> <br /> As for the Furies, there was never a Birth disparity. They utilized strong relationships with other tribes to maintain numbers and 'balance'. Male Garou went to CoG, sometimes other tribes. They took in a disproportionate number of female lost cubs and occasional other converts.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jobs are simply human jobs each auspice of a tribe can do in the human world. Given the role of kinfolk, and Rage, I rather dislike them being just randomly listed.<br /> <br /> The Bitten are kinfolk or Lost Cubs who, due to a bite from a garou, turn into garou.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T17:29:14-08:00","id":1055901,"title":"","content":"I'm all for more conflict within the Garou Nation, but drawing an arbitrary line down the middle of it seems kinda ridiculous. I also don't get why the Glasswalkers would go all Cyberdog again having just expended no small effort in purging them. <br /> <br /> I'll admit I actually really like all the Bitten stuff, but I'm also not really part of Werewolf's core fanbase so I wouldn't be surprised to meet disagreement on that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T17:41:55-08:00","id":1055909,"title":"","content":"Jobs - I'm not too fazed by this part. Larp is all about social interaction, so maybe they are toning down the effects of Rage on normal people? More curious about the list honestly.<br /> <br /> Bitten - my first reactions is NOPE NOPE NOPE. This blurs the line between Kin and Garou and could cause all sorts of crazy drama. After my first reaction faded, I will reserver judgement until I read the section and see what limits are on it. I assume it's not &quot;You got bit, you become Garou!&quot;<br /> <br /> I don't want to get into the split between the tribes. I liked the tribes working as individual groups instead of &quot;I'm a tradition Garou!&quot; &quot;I'm a progressive Garou!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 02-27-2017, 08:46 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T20:49:25-08:00","id":1055971,"title":"","content":"Quite a few of these changes I can get behind. A method to have a Garou first change somewhere other than puberty opens quite a few doors. I am hoping it's not just some random thing though, because this would mean sickies during coitus create Metis. Jobs sounds awkward. Like a soldier having to make sure he finishes a battle quickly so he can be home in time to shower, change, and flip burgers.<br /> <br /> Fewer Caerns is something I've always believed in, and 'protectorates' like were seen in Rage Across New York got a little more screen time from me. Previous authors and developers have talked about there being as few as 3 per continent, in order to keep them special and valuable. However, that ran into the issue of 'everybody wants one in their home town'. While I would never have gone that low myself, gateways into the spirit world should be relatively rare and valuable, and not within easy walking distance of each other. (And this is before taking into account the other game lines that have similar places.)<br /> <br /> \u200bDid Stargazers come back from the Beast Courts? Or did they never leave in the LARP setting? Basically it boiled down to 'the Tribal Elders got fed up, and stopped coming to the meetings' (which had exactly as much impact on the PCs and Story as the players wanted them to have.) If anything, I would have used their departure as the springboard for the split rather than retcon it out.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5818-eviltyger","name":"EvilTyger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5818_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"314"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T21:23:09-08:00","id":1055979,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>EvilTyger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1055971#post1055971\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quite a few of these changes I can get behind. A method to have a Garou first change somewhere other than puberty opens quite a few doors. I am hoping it's not just some random thing though, because this would mean sickies during coitus create Metis.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's already a pretty big danger in the setting as presented, though, since W20 presents it as &quot;you can't tell if someone is a pre-Change Garou or if they're kinfolk&quot;, and not everyone does change on time...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Jobs sounds awkward. Like a soldier having to make sure he finishes a battle quickly so he can be home in time to shower, change, and flip burgers. </div> </div> </div>Especially since he has a set of inhuman drives that would make being motivated for a typical job... difficult, to say the least.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Fewer Caerns is something I've always believed in, and 'protectorates' like were seen in Rage Across New York got a little more screen time from me. Previous authors and developers have talked about there being as few as 3 per continent, in order to keep them special and valuable. However, that ran into the issue of 'everybody wants one in their home town'. While I would never have gone that low myself, gateways into the spirit world should be relatively rare and valuable, and not within easy walking distance of each other. (And this is before taking into account the other game lines that have similar places.) </div> </div> </div>On the other hand, the BNS game bent over backwards to make the Umbra inaccessible, like it's some kind of vanilla alternate universe instead of the soul of the world. It also had some weird things about the Gauntlet being impassible for Gaian changers in Wyrm caerns... even though that has never been a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T23:18:24-08:00","id":1056000,"title":"","content":"So is this supposed to be the &quot;new&quot; setting for NuWW?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-27T23:47:37-08:00","id":1056002,"title":"","content":"That's not entirely clear. But the BNS WtA MET book was supposed to be made with a lot of input from WW regarding the direction the 5e books are going to take.<br /> <br /> We have no idea how closely WtA 5e will hew to BNS version of things (considering how far in the future it will be), but it's a fair assumption to see it as the direction WW plans on taking with the setting. The broader the strokes the more likely things are to be true (so it's very high probability that WtA 5e will maintain the 'Age of the Apocalypse' thing where it turns out instead of one cataclysmic event the war's going to last a long time, but we could easily see a lot of the small details change).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T01:30:59-08:00","id":1056020,"title":"","content":"Has By Night I said anything about doing Mage next?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T03:26:42-08:00","id":1056040,"title":"","content":"Stargazers came back with their Beast Court allies all victorious. Which to me, and this is purely just my personal bias, really does not feel justified. One of my favourite things about Stargazers revised tb, was that for all their talk of being more civilized and in-tune with themselves, they were still Garou Nation garou. They were trying to join a culture that had had unity for centuries and did not behave like the Nation, and it was clearly hard. The Fera section is full of basically 'can't trust these guys' mentality, the Beast Courts don't really trust them and they generally feel ill-fit among them.<br /> <br /> Basically, it addressed very well the issues of trying to force yourself into another culture and what it can result in. Gazers ended up basically as outsiders because they weren't the civilized tribe they thought they were.<br /> <br /> To have them come back with allies all victorious, and their numbers swelled by Mongolian wolves, it undercuts the message of the revised book.<br /> <br /> Anyway, to the Bitten, it seems to function very similarly to the Birth Plague of the Ratkin. It needs a bite and then ties to the garou by blood. Most die from it, and a child being Bitten will only change once as an adult.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T05:02:46-08:00","id":1056061,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1055808#post1055808\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note: Glasswalker is my favorite tribe.<br /> <br /> I kind of hate how Glasswalkers are all &quot;Weaver good/Wyld bad.&quot; While I believe that is how the rest of the Garou nation sees Glasswalkers, I feel they see Weaver as a Tool and something to be controlled, rather than a preference over the Wyld.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Revised tribebook went quite a bit from there thankfuly. Alas, most people go by the Urrah moniker and the internet stereotype. I still break out in hives whenever someone believes that everything is serving and being of a single member of the Triat. If you do, you're an insane nutter, not a playable PC.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T06:56:58-08:00","id":1056089,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056040#post1056040\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyway, to the Bitten, it seems to function very similarly to the Birth Plague of the Ratkin. It needs a bite and then ties to the garou by blood. Most die from it, and a child being Bitten will only change once as an adult.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. So I've slept on the concept and the Bitten thing is weird but passes my &quot;Can I make an interesting character from this?&quot; test.<br /> <br /> At first I was like &quot;Wolves aren't plague carriers like rats!&quot; but then I remember Rabies. As long as the Garou has some control over if their bite passes on the curse. Lovebites from your Garou mate shouldn't curse you to either death or divorce. If you get bit by a Garou in Frenzy, you are cursed. I have this image of a Garou foaming from the mouth in preparation of the bite curse. Or maybe the curse is only passed by Crinos bites, which makes the situation more tragic for Metis pups. (This is the one reason I wouldn't use the concept in my game. Things are already tragic enough for Metis pups.)<br /> <br /> The character concept I got from this was the youngest child of a Breed 5 Garou. All of her children ended up Kinfolk, so you were her last hope of having a Garou child to pass on her legacy to. Yet you were an easygoing child. Not prone to anger. You had none of the stereotypical hallmarks of a child that will go though their first change. One night, while you slept a monster visited you. Your mother sank her teeth into your side. After that you remember nothing but fevered dreams of battle and wolves. You father and stepmother never forgave your mother for what she did, but as you survived and became Garou, she felt she did what was right.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T07:08:20-08:00","id":1056092,"title":"","content":"Also, what makes the setting &quot;post-apocalypse&quot;? I'm assuming we aren't talking Mad Max here and the world isn't much different than today's society. Did the Wyld fall the to Weaver? Is the splitting of the Garou Nation considered the Apocalypse?<br /> <br /> Also, are we talking about<a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/195992/Minds-Eye-Theatre-Werewolf-The-Apocalypse?src=newest\" target=\"_blank\"> this book?</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":3950,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","user":"wonderandawe","date":". 02-28-2017, 10:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T07:17:46-08:00","id":1056098,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056092#post1056092\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, what makes the setting &quot;post-apocalypse&quot;? I'm assuming we aren't talking Mad Max here and the world isn't much different than today's society. Did the Wyld fall the to Weaver? Is the splitting of the Garou Nation considered the Apocalypse?<br /> <br /> Also, are we talking about<a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/195992/Minds-Eye-Theatre-Werewolf-The-Apocalypse?src=newest\" target=\"_blank\"> this book?</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, that IS the book.<br /> <br /> For the bite, it is literally -any- bite from a garou, it seems.<br /> <br /> The setting is post-apocalypse in a sense that there are only 13 caerns, the gauntlet is thick and lots of garou have died, plus the Nation has split.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T07:39:50-08:00","id":1056106,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056098#post1056098\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the bite, it is literally -any- bite from a garou, it seems.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd probably house rule that to Crinos bites, which would leave scars on the Garou marking them as Bitten.<br /> <br /> Though the whole situation does beg this question. If only kinfolk children can be turned into Garou via bite, then maybe the reason why only some kids survive is that they are already destined to be Garou?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T07:53:07-08:00","id":1056109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056106#post1056106\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd probably house rule that to Crinos bites, which would leave scars on the Garou marking them as Bitten.<br /> <br /> Though the whole situation does beg this question. If only kinfolk children can be turned into Garou via bite, then maybe the reason why only some kids survive is that they are already destined to be Garou?</div> </div> </div> </div>These are mostly adults, note. Children cannot get turned, until they grow up. Which to me is a bit silly. WtA has metis all ready, children with shitty lives is part of the canon. So kids getting bit? Fits right in to the theme.<br /> <br /> Of course, ooc, this thing is used to justify the aging LARP crowd. And I get that. But later First Changes could have helped.<br /> <br /> Though, I admit if BSDs know of this it is fun times for the Nation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T08:00:59-08:00","id":1056115,"title":"","content":"I'm going to stop nitpicking a book I haven't bought yet. I still got all my W20 stuff to play with. Is there more W20 stuff coming down the pipeline? <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T08:01:38-08:00","id":1056116,"title":"","content":"Not a huge fan of the bitten concept but it isn't enough to turn me away. I do dislike the attempt to turn the Garou tribes into Cammarilla/Sabbat lines.<br /> <br /> \u200bI fully support males being added into Black Furies. They are my least favorite tribe due to being misandrist bigots at worst and bigots at best. It's exactly like the Get taking steps to purge the Nazi minded from their midst.<br /> <br /> \u200bI don't like the GW's direction either. It was fine as one minor element of the greater piece but not as a defining characteristic of the tribe. I also don't like the change to the gauntlet and caerns.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'm not extremely optimistic about NuWtA in light of this information, but I'll wait and see how the core TT book ends up being before I make any final judgments.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12474-cavebear56","name":"cavebear56","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T08:05:33-08:00","id":1056118,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056115#post1056115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm going to stop nitpicking a book I haven't bought yet. I still got all my W20 stuff to play with. Is there more W20 stuff coming down the pipeline?</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, W20 stuff should keep coming just fine. Changing Ways, tribebook: Bunyip are the ones I remember on the top of my head.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T08:07:58-08:00","id":1056119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>cavebear56</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056116#post1056116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">\u200bI fully support males being added into Black Furies. They are my least favorite tribe due to being misandrist bigots at worst and bigots at best. It's exactly like the Get taking steps to purge the Nazi minded from their midst.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Black Fury tribe to include Males is one of the changes I agree with (though the birth rate reasoning is stupid) and they are one of my favorite tribes. You don't have to have a vagina to understand the power of female principle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T08:30:01-08:00","id":1056131,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056119#post1056119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Black Fury tribe to include Males is one of the changes I agree with (though the birth rate reasoning is stupid) and they are one of my favorite tribes. You don't have to have a vagina to understand the power of female principle.</div> </div> </div> </div>To me, it just feels rather like letting majority into a space meant for minorities. Why should they add males to be more open minded?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T09:04:06-08:00","id":1056135,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1055861#post1055861\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As in, each tribe's auspice lists what jobs they would do in the human world. Bear in mind that this includes ahroun and galliards.</div> </div> </div> </div>I dont mind this personally, to me if a PC wants to have a job i would let them (as long as it makes sense) but i was never a fan on the whole concept of &quot;bums garous who only live to fight&quot;.<br /> <br /> That said, the list of jobs must be pretty tight and carefully selected.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1055901#post1055901\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm all for more conflict within the Garou Nation, but drawing an arbitrary line down the middle of it seems kinda ridiculous. I also don't get why the Glasswalkers would go all Cyberdog again having just expended no small effort in purging them.<br /> <br /> I'll admit I actually really like all the Bitten stuff, but I'm also not really part of Werewolf's core fanbase so I wouldn't be surprised to meet disagreement on that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Its not really a arbitrary line more than the garou nation divide themselves between political correct/neutral tribes and non-politically correct tribes.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1055836#post1055836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sanctum of Gaia: Black Furies, Fianna, Get of Fenris, Red Talons, Silver Fangs and Wendigo</div> </div> </div> </div>This are the tribes considered for many as the racist, ableist, homophobic, misandrous, elitist and genocidal and all around problematic if a deeper reading isnt made.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1055836#post1055836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Concordiat of the Stars: Bone Gnawers, Glass Walkers, Children of Gaia, Shadow Lords, Stargazers and Uktena</div> </div> </div> </div>And this ones are the normally considered &quot;good guys&quot; tribes. Personally if this is the direction Werewolf is taking, unless the mechanics are good and i can use them and ignore the fluff i would give the whole game a pass. This division is unecesary and run counter with what i think is the whole point of werewolf, that you HAVE to interact and work with the asshole tribes. But the good tribes making their own clubhouse diminish that a lot, transform the asshole tribes in &quot;the other&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","user":"LokiRavenSpeak","date":". 02-28-2017, 12:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T09:53:02-08:00","id":1056164,"title":"","content":"Re-quoting the tribal divisions just to keep this part of the conversation straight.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1055836#post1055836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Sanctum of Gaia: Black Furies, Fianna, Get of Fenris, Red Talons, Silver Fangs and Wendigo</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056135#post1056135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> This are the tribes considered for many as the racist, ableist, homophobic, misandrous, elitist and genocidal and all around problematic if a deeper reading isnt made.</div> </div> </div> </div>While I can almost see your point here, it's really odd to me to have this section of tribes grouped together, given how much animosity there was between some of these tribes. It's not like the &quot;asshole tribes&quot; every got along with each other. If anything, they tended to dislike each other a hell of a lot more (the Fury-Get relationship comes to mind most immediately). I can see the Talons siding with the Silver Fangs. That's kind of always been that way. But I don't see the Wendigo falling in line with them and going against the Uktena. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1055836#post1055836\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Concordiat of the Stars: Bone Gnawers, Glass Walkers, Children of Gaia, Shadow Lords, Stargazers and Uktena</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056135#post1056135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And this ones are the normally considered &quot;good guys&quot; tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know that I've ever heard the Shadow Lords being referred to as &quot;good guys&quot; before <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> This really does seem like an attempt at setting up a Camarilla/Sabbat dynamic. Which wasn't necessary in WtA at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056135#post1056135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Personally if this is the direction Werewolf is taking, unless the mechanics are good and i can use them and ignore the fluff i would give the whole game a pass. This division is unecesary and run counter with what i think is the whole point of werewolf, that you HAVE to interact and work with the asshole tribes. But the good tribes making their own clubhouse diminish that a lot, transform the asshole tribes in &quot;the other&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. This division seems more than a bit pointless. I will probably also just ignore the fluff if the rest of the line is good. I feel like this is taking several steps back from the progress they made with Revised.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T10:51:27-08:00","id":1056201,"title":"","content":"God, I hadn't thought about Werewolf in forever. I'm getting nostalgic now. As far as these political/social changes, a lot of them worry me. It's not that I necessarily dislike all the ideas in theory, but more that the way they've been framed here simplifies things in a manner that doesn't really appeal to me. Granted, I haven't actually read the book yet, so I could be misinterpreting. From the sound of things, a lot of garou have been died, and traveling between caerns is a lot more difficult, so I'd imagine we'd see a more fractured political structure with a younger guard making decisions and regional decisions taking precedence over tribe-wide decisions. But for instance...<br /> <br /> I like the idea of more inclusive Black Furies, but only if there's still conflict within that idea instead of just &quot;Well, we're accepting men now&quot;. It strikes me as a good reflection of where feminism is today. With resources drawn thinner, there'd probably be more arguments about how the specific interests of women of color and other marginalized groups are prioritized in comparison to &quot;universal&quot; issues (that have a tendency to be more white people problems). And I can't doubt queerness would be a part of that discussion. Where do non-binary and trans people fit into the BF perspective on femininity? And if they're allowing men into the tribe, what are their criteria, and is their hierarchy? Feminism today is a very split and complicated philosophy, and I think that makes interesting fodder for the tribe.<br /> <br /> Similarly the Get of Fenris. With a lot of discussions about &quot;heritage not hate&quot; and the increased prominence of nationalism, ethnic supremacy, and alpha male nostalgia, I could see a resurgence of traditionalism for the reformers in the tribe to deal with.<br /> <br /> I'll admit I'm not a big fan of the &quot;Walkers are team Weaver&quot; bit or the &quot;Camarilla/Sabbat&quot; split (as Loki said). It doesn't seem practical to me to have two camps split across these clean delineations. A two party system makes sense for Vampire, but it's much less so for Werewolf. I'd look at the splintering among leftists as a better parallel: where you have everything from classical liberals to MLMs to tankies and varying degrees of respect and disgust between them depending on where their ideologies lie. Given the other changes they seem to be making to the setting, I think a regional rather than top-down approach to how politics works makes a lot more sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T11:20:11-08:00","id":1056230,"title":"","content":"Agreeing with most of this but picking out a specific thing in the Black Fury paragraph to reply to for brevity:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056201#post1056201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And I can't doubt queerness would be a part of that discussion. Where do non-binary and trans people fit into the BF perspective on femininity?</div> </div> </div> </div>A while back there was a really good thread (mostly) on Black Fury and trans Tribemates. It can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals#post977995\">here</a>. It got pretty long (18 pages) but stayed surprisingly civil for the majority of it. Lots of great points made I think. Certainly worth a read if anyone is interested and has the time. I'm guessing it handles to topic a lot better than the books are going to (if they go into it at all).<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T11:41:28-08:00","id":1056247,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056230#post1056230\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreeing with most of this but picking out a specific thing in the Black Fury paragraph to reply to for brevity:<br /> <br /> <br /> A while back there was a really good thread (mostly) on Black Fury and trans Tribemates. It can be found <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/977995-black-furies-and-transgender-individuals#post977995\">here</a>. It got pretty long (18 pages) but stayed surprisingly civil for the majority of it. Lots of great points made I think. Certainly worth a read if anyone is interested and has the time. I'm guessing it handles to topic a lot better than the books are going to (if they go into it at all).</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Interesting! I'll have to check that out, thanks.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I'd assume there's a strong contingent of TERFs in the Black Furies, and I think the identity politics splits between different members of the tribe could make for some really interesting fodder.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T11:41:36-08:00","id":1056248,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056164#post1056164\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I can almost see your point here, it's really odd to me to have this section of tribes grouped together, given how much animosity there was between some of these tribes. It's not like the &quot;asshole tribes&quot; every got along with each other. If anything, they tended to dislike each other a hell of a lot more (the Fury-Get relationship comes to mind most immediately). I can see the Talons siding with the Silver Fangs. That's kind of always been that way. But I don't see the Wendigo falling in line with them and going against the Uktena.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed. I really can't see the Wendigo shacking up with a band made of Get, Fianna, and Silver Fangs. That just seems so incredibly far-fetched to me.<br /> <br /> More of a general comment here:<br /> From what I've heard so far in interviews, WtA 5e will likely be including some big changes within the Nation. The video game is bringing home the question of, &quot;Will a human apocalypse help prevent OUR apocalypse?&quot; The Nation is fairly split on that question, from the sound of it, and the above groupings could fit into, &quot;Yes, let's do it,&quot; and a, &quot;No, are you nuts?&quot; camps. Considering this Garou Nation split is the direction of both MET and the video game, it's likely that this may be 5e's overall direction too. Perhaps the video game is a prelude to how 5e's world will be.<br /> <br /> Frankly, I'm not a big fan of two-party dynamic wars. One big group, three or more factions, you have fun things to do there. Two PC groups going head-to-head all the time gets boring really quickly, in my opinion (WoW is a shining example of, &quot;Really? Do we even know why the hell we're fighting anymore, especially when half the time we're still working together anyway?&quot;) Some Tribes are already blacklisted at many tables because of their &quot;can't get along with others&quot; mentality (e.g. the Talons and the Wendigo), and I feel that does a disservice to what the game really offers for role-playing opportunities. Creating this rift is going to limit future pack dynamics even more.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12777-wakuwa","name":"Wakuwa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12777_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"37"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T12:53:09-08:00","id":1056286,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056119#post1056119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Black Fury tribe to include Males is one of the changes I agree with (though the birth rate reasoning is stupid) and they are one of my favorite tribes. You don't have to have a vagina to understand the power of female principle.</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bCompletely agree with your entire comment. Outside of literally giving birth, a Black Fury shows no traits that men do not also have. Caring about equality and being kind aren't sole traits tied to women.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056131#post1056131\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To me, it just feels rather like letting majority into a space meant for minorities. Why should they add males to be more open minded?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bWhy shouldn't they? Diversity is the spice of life and by denying males is to be close minded and exclusionary. By adding men they already open the floodgates to allow more open mindedness because otherwise you get stuck with a gaggle of groupthink (in this example the feminist agenda who craft an echo chamber). That isn't growth nor a component for open mindedness. I'm not a fan of anybody having their own space because it reeks of segregation to me (something I'm not a fan of). Just because one may be a part of a majority doesn't mean they should be treated any worse, or better, than a minority.<br /> <br /> \u200bI'll leave it at this though as I don't want to derail this topic into something that won't allow it to grow.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12474-cavebear56","name":"cavebear56","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T13:52:26-08:00","id":1056311,"title":"","content":"I think part of the problem is that &quot;minority&quot; spaces aren't meant to be 100% exclusive. They're mean to be places where minorities don't have to feel like minorities.<br /> <br /> Allowing members of the majority in isn't a &quot;violation&quot; of that space as long as that member of the majority respects that space.<br /> <br /> For example, there's a Christian member of my synagogue. She's not converting, or anything like that. She's not their to appropriate Jewish culture in some weird fashion. She's there because she wanted to learn, and stayed part of the community after. She enjoys participating on the level she can without being disrespectful. She insist on Christian things being brought in, or accommodation made for her beliefs.<br /> <br /> The Black Furies having men in their ranks is acknowledging the same ability for allies to be in minority spaces by earning their status as allies. Male Black Furies are raised or taught how to fight for equality and respect how to be allies instead of white-knights.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T14:34:24-08:00","id":1056323,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> , <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12474-cavebear56\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12474\" data-vbnamecard=\"12474\">cavebear56</a> Yeah, you bring up good points. As long as it is done well and with a good explanation, I wouldn't mind.<br /> <br /> There are other things too, Fianna angered their Fae allies and now they lack them, Bone Gnawers are now middle-class/working class. The Gnawers thing I don't mind, but poor Fianna.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T14:59:11-08:00","id":1056330,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056323#post1056323\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a> , <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12474-cavebear56\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12474\" data-vbnamecard=\"12474\">cavebear56</a> Yeah, you bring up good points. As long as it is done well and with a good explanation, I wouldn't mind.<br /> <br /> There are other things too, Fianna angered their Fae allies and now they lack them, Bone Gnawers are now middle-class/working class. The Gnawers thing I don't mind, but poor Fianna.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh man. They fixed Fianna with focusing on their Fae connections and now they broke the tribe again!<br /> <br /> Is there a Fianna character concept that can't be played by having an Irish Sliver Fang, Bone Gnawer, or Get of Fenrir? I guess you can play up the Bard aspect of the tribe. *shrug*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T15:04:37-08:00","id":1056335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056201#post1056201\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Similarly the Get of Fenris. With a lot of discussions about &quot;heritage not hate&quot; and the increased prominence of nationalism, ethnic supremacy, and alpha male nostalgia, I could see a resurgence of traditionalism for the reformers in the tribe to deal with.</div> </div> </div> </div>They, ah, already dealt with that contingent, back in the Revised tribebook. The Swords of Heimdall are dead, and anyone who sympathized with them isn't in a position to make their sympathies known.<br /> <br /> Of course, why the Get would even care about being &quot;Nordic&quot; or not is perplexing, since the entire culture of vikings, which venerated Odin, Woden, Wotan or whatever, was their enemy. They, at best, had their kin give lip service to the pagan North European &quot;deities&quot; to avoid becoming targets, and they basically sat back and smiled with Christianity absorbed and destroyed their enemies in those communities.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'll admit I'm not a big fan of the &quot;Walkers are team Weaver&quot; bit or the &quot;Camarilla/Sabbat&quot; split (as Loki said). It doesn't seem practical to me to have two camps split across these clean delineations. A two party system makes sense for Vampire, but it's much less so for Werewolf. I'd look at the splintering among leftists as a better parallel: where you have everything from classical liberals to MLMs to tankies and varying degrees of respect and disgust between them depending on where their ideologies lie. Given the other changes they seem to be making to the setting, I think a regional rather than top-down approach to how politics works makes a lot more sense. </div> </div> </div>The fact that it also has tribal weaknesses serves to hammer home BNS Werewolf being too close to Vampire. Why two divisions? Because Vampire did it. Why tribal weaknesses? Because Vampire had clan weaknesses. Why have characters with normal day jobs and the ability to conceal what they are? Why shut out the Umbra?<br /> <br /> At some point, a different game needs to be different, and BNS Werewolf is far, far past that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T15:36:01-08:00","id":1056344,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056330#post1056330\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh man. They fixed Fianna with focusing on their Fae connections and now they broke the tribe again!<br /> <br /> Is there a Fianna character concept that can't be played by having an Irish Sliver Fang, Bone Gnawer, or Get of Fenrir? I guess you can play up the Bard aspect of the tribe. *shrug*</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, so much agree here. The fae things is interesting, and it can be very dark. I mean, there ARE Seelie Redcaps.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T15:54:05-08:00","id":1056354,"title":"","content":"Did the Fianna keep their anti-Metis and rather oddly ableist view? That was one thing I ALWAYS hated, and when I played a Fianna I made it a huge point to be against in his background. The tribe includes the story of Nuada and his amputation which costs him his as High King that is then handed over to a Fomor sympathizer who betrays the tribe and messes the Fianna over....yet they still keep their odd (rather anti-Garou &quot;oh you lost your arm in a battle to save Gaia, too bad can't be an Alpha now!&quot;) perfect mind perfect body garbage. Again, I can't emphasize how much I despised that aspect of the tribe....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1179,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","user":"CeltSPZ","date":". 02-28-2017, 07:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T16:01:21-08:00","id":1056357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056354#post1056354\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did the Fianna keep their anti-Metis and rather oddly ableist view? That was one thing I ALWAYS hated, and when I played a Fianna I made it a huge point to be against in his background. The tribe includes the story of Noada and his amputation which costs him his as High King that is then handed over to a Fomor sympathizer who betrays the tribe and messes the Fianna over....yet they still keep their odd (rather anti-Garou &quot;oh you lost your arm in a battle to save Gaia, too bad can't be an Alpha now!&quot;) perfect mind perfect body garbage. Again, I can't emphasize how much I despised that aspect of the tribe....</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <i>&quot;Fianna Metis are<br /> seen by their tribe as a constant reminder of the choice<br /> that two Garou made to forsake the Litany. Fianna rarely<br /> take in Metis, even their own, and barely tolerate them in<br /> septs and packs. Every mistake a Metis makes is mocked<br /> and punished; every chance for expulsion is exploited.<br /> Metis are not family.&quot; <b>MET WtA, p.82</b></i><br /> <br /> So, yep. In fact business as usual with the last part.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T16:14:36-08:00","id":1056365,"title":"","content":"People at least understand my issue with this part of the tribe right? <br /> If ableism messed your tribe over and was the reason for the 2nd Battle of Moy Tara that (debatably) almost ended your tribe...you think you'd learn (Nuada the High King loses his arm in battle...and has to leave the position, which is then offered to a beautiful (but tainted) successor.....its been a huge pet peeve of just stupidity).<br /> To be a warrior species, who is all about the grand sacrifice, but man, if you lost an arm or something to save Gaia...you better die too because you come back seen as unfit to hold any leadership position.....given the bulk of Garou culture and their views on battle scars its just SO CONTRARY TO IT","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T16:35:00-08:00","id":1056368,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056311#post1056311\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Black Furies having men in their ranks is acknowledging the same ability for allies to be in minority spaces by earning their status as allies. Male Black Furies are raised or taught how to fight for equality and respect how to be allies instead of white-knights.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's a question of recognizing the inherently self-destructive hypocrisies of the world. I think most of us recognize that inclusiveness is important, but that doesn't mean the establishment necessarily does, and creating a tribe that is at odds with traditionalism and progressivism creates more interesting internal conflict.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">They, ah, already dealt with that contingent, back in the Revised tribebook. The Swords of Heimdall are dead, and anyone who sympathized with them isn't in a position to make their sympathies known.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I recognize that. But I think current trends in the real world can add a new wrinkle. If the Revised setting was about how the Get had purged the racists, purists, and extremists from their ranks, or at least shushed them into silence, 5E can be about how these things are cyclical -- about garou politics reflecting the rising tide of nationalism, conservatism, and racial identity that's becoming frighteningly more prominent in the public consciousness.<br /> <br /> It sounds like they might be angling towards a setting that wipes some of the barnacles from the underside of the ship. The tribes and the garou as a whole are decimated, largely under the direction of younger members, and desperately backed against the wall. This allows for radical changes, but there's opposing ideologies, and any of these tribes could tip one way or another.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T22:08:48-08:00","id":1056483,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056368#post1056368\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think it's a question of recognizing the inherently self-destructive hypocrisies of the world. I think most of us recognize that inclusiveness is important, but that doesn't mean the establishment necessarily does, and creating a tribe that is at odds with traditionalism and progressivism creates more interesting internal conflict.<br /> <br /> Oh, I recognize that. But I think current trends in the real world can add a new wrinkle. If the Revised setting was about how the Get had purged the racists, purists, and extremists from their ranks, or at least shushed them into silence, 5E can be about how these things are cyclical -- about garou politics reflecting the rising tide of nationalism, conservatism, and racial identity that's becoming frighteningly more prominent in the public consciousness.</div> </div> </div> </div>And why would monsters necessarily follow human cultural trends? It could be that the Get's problem is in making too obvious bloody messes of modern fascists, not that they're siding with them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It sounds like they might be angling towards a setting that wipes some of the barnacles from the underside of the ship. The tribes and the garou as a whole are decimated, largely under the direction of younger members, and desperately backed against the wall. This allows for radical changes, but there's opposing ideologies, and any of these tribes could tip one way or another. </div> </div> </div>That wasn't the direction it was moving in during Revised, though. Everything in BNS is from out of nowhere and often relies on prior editions' material, skipping entirely over Revised.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-28T23:48:59-08:00","id":1056508,"title":"","content":"I really dislike the shoehorning of men into the Black Furies. They aren't a tribe about equality or even hating men, they are about solely focusing on the feminine and are a Wyld worshipping fertility cult with a focus on meting out justice for historically vulnerable groups (women and children). If you want to play a Homid don't try to be a Red Talon. If you want to play a white person don't try to be a Wendigo or Uktena. If you want a male Fury be a Metis. It takes away from the identity of the tribes.<br /> <br /> <br /> When I hear a lot of complaints about the Furies it's typically from male players. Here's my totally biased armchair bitch fest but the guys who I have personally spoken to who complain about the tribe usually list that their excluding men is unfair and that men can seek justice too. That isn't the point and it makes a tribe of women into &quot;but what about the men?&quot; and &quot;not all men.&quot; It's like they take offense for being excluded when they are used to not only being included in almost everything but being the center of attention. <br /> <br /> <br /> Women have had a pretty shit hand dealt to them through most of human history and the Black Furies are a fictionalization of the concept of &quot;what if?&quot; &quot;What if women could have had a say in their role in society, stood up for themselves, owned their own bodies, were allowed agency over themselves?&quot; You don't have to force men into the tribe for the sake of fairness because it was never meant to be fair.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3198-lunar-falcon","name":"Lunar Falcon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3198_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"103"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T00:12:18-08:00","id":1056513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056483#post1056483\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And why would monsters necessarily follow human cultural trends? It could be that the Get's problem is in making too obvious bloody messes of modern fascists, not that they're siding with them.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> That wasn't the direction it was moving in during Revised, though. Everything in BNS is from out of nowhere and often relies on prior editions' material, skipping entirely over Revised.</div> </div> </div> </div>They wouldn't NECESSARILY follow human cultural trends (and if that's not the route you'd want to take, it's perfectly valid), but I see a couple of reasons why it would make sense to take that route, and why it's a direction I personally prefer.<br /> <br /> From a lore perspective, it makes sense. These are creatures who live half in the world of man and half in the spiritual. Who they were before their first change informs who they become. The attitudes of their kinfolk and the other people they see in their daily lives influences their decisions, and the political and social attitudes of the mortal climate creates opportunities.<br /> <br /> In more meta terms, I like my games to be a reflection of the reality I know, and a way of exploring that reality in interesting ways. Especially in modern games, I look for concepts that reflect my lived reality, warts and all, and I think looking for those kinds of patterns is an inherently human thing, and a core virtue of storytelling in general. If there's a tribe of fiercely female warrior women, I see fertile ground of allegory for the feminist struggles I see in the groups I run in. When I see the Get, I see a reflection of military warrior culture and the reflectively hostile insularity of much of modern far right conservatism (and admittedly, my opinion is probably the outlier here, and I'm not expecting the writers to create a game tailored to my preferences). For me, at least, Werewolf is very much a game about the safety of the past: the threat of a mythical history that obfuscates the troubles that past represented, and the inability to achieve that in the face of an uncertain and frightening future. It's not the major theme for me (that would likely be the dual natured romance and dangers of radical ideology and the questions of moral righteousness when faced with an unbeatable threat), but it's prominent; and, as much as I abhor and pity the rising prominence of vaguely fascist nationalism, I think there's a stark metaphor in those people's apocalyptic view of the future, a future where they see their values, or religion, or racial identity, or whatever, threatened by existential genocide.<br /> <br /> In regards to the new writers skipping right over Revised, not gonna argue with you there. That sucks, and I'll be honest, I don't find a lot of these ideas, as presented, as very palatable. That said, it's been over a decade now. If the writers decided they wanted to undertake some rather major retcons for the sake of a bold new setting, I wouldn't be adverse to that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But again, these changes don't indicate an edition that's going to appeal to me.<br /> <br /> I'm curious about your thoughts though. How do you perceive the Get? What's their hook for you? And how would you like to see them develop in 5e? It's been quite a few years, so there's a lot of possibilities for how they might have evolved.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 03-01-2017, 03:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T01:59:29-08:00","id":1056538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lunar Falcon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056508#post1056508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They aren't a tribe about equality or even hating men, they are about solely focusing on the feminine and are a Wyld worshipping fertility cult with a focus on meting out justice for historically vulnerable groups (women and children).</div> </div> </div> </div>If they aren't a Tribe about equality, why are they wasting their meting out justice for the historically vulnerable groups? We already have the Bone Gnawers, Children of Gaia, and Uktena that have &quot;mete out justice for the disenfranchised,&quot; as part of their shtick anyway. There's also a lot to answer for in their old traditions of killing babies for having a penis; kinda hard to mete out justice for children when you kill your male children that so the signs of becoming Garou to maintain the illusion that Black Furies don't give birth to male Garou kids. Their refusal (until the BNS changes) to stand up for gay men, queer anything that's not female, or transgender people doesn't exactly show them as champions of the historically vulnerable either.<br /> <br /> If they're a Wyld worshiping fertility cult, why exclude men? Werewolves can't reproduce asexually, so they need both sets of parts to celebrate fertility. Real world matriarchal fertility religions don't show any evidence of excluding men from being active participants just because of their focus on femininity as the core of fertility. If you're out to maximize fertility in the setting, you want male kin to knock up female Garou, and male Garou to knock up female kin. Excluding that second part for just kin-kin pairs doesn't make sense.<br /> <br /> The problem is that, like many of the Tribes, the Black Furies were designed as political message first, and the authors have been back-filling and retconning in material to try to have them make sense. They started as a fantasy fulfillment of the late second wave/proto-third wave feminist ass-kickers. This included all the problematic issues with prescriptive femininity simply being moved from patriarchy to matriarchy instead of self-definition, and a lot of TERF nonsense. Everything meant to expand them past that (like the whole Wyld worshiping fertility cult stuff) was added later to make a bit more than the early dull stereotype, however as they added such things, the reasoning behind them being AFAB only diminished. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you want to play a Homid don't try to be a Red Talon. </div> </div> </div>Personally, I've always found this to be stupid. But my dislike of the Red Talons is far deeper than this and not worth getting into here. Needless to say, the idea that the Red Talons reject Homids that want to reject their humanity is an entirely too human way of thinking for a Tribe that's all wolves IMO.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you want to play a white person don't try to be a Wendigo or Uktena. </div> </div> </div>Kind of a funny statement given characters like Evan Heals the Past being long standing canon characters. It seems like the authors didn't want to exclude, &quot;playing a white person that finds out they had some tiny amount of indigenous people in them and wants to connect with that heritage,&quot; as something these Tribes deal with.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If you want a male Fury be a Metis. </div> </div> </div>You realize this was a change introduced later in the game, right? Originally this wasn't even a possibility.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It takes away from the identity of the tribes. </div> </div> </div>Does it? I'll admit in some cases it makes justifying all the Tribes as separate entities difficult (but I think that's an issue with a lot of the Tribes overlapping way too much anyway). But one person's dilution the Tribe's identity is another person's expansion of it. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> When I hear a lot of complaints about the Furies it's typically from male players. </div> </div> </div>Would you like me to get my wife to post her standard rant on everything wrong with the Black Furies? You'll have to trust it's her posting via my account, but I'm pretty sure she'll oblige if you really want. Though we share very similar opinions about them, and you seem very focused on one complaint to the exclusion of all the far more compelling ones.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Women have had a pretty shit hand dealt to them through most of human history and the Black Furies are a fictionalization of the concept of &quot;what if?&quot; &quot;What if women could have had a say in their role in society, stood up for themselves, owned their own bodies, were allowed agency over themselves?&quot; You don't have to force men into the tribe for the sake of fairness because it was never meant to be fair. </div> </div> </div>This never addresses why outright excluding them in the first place was the right idea. You don't need an all female (and worse all AFAB) group to answer the &quot;What if&quot; posed. A matriarchal Tribe that excepts all genders and sexes can still explore these topics.<br /> <br /> Of course, it all seems like a strawman to me, because I've seen a lot of complaints about the Furies - both idiotic and well thought out - but &quot;it's not fair for them to exclude men!&quot; has never been one of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T02:08:02-08:00","id":1056540,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056365#post1056365\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People at least understand my issue with this part of the tribe right?<br /> If ableism messed your tribe over and was the reason for the 2nd Battle of Moy Tara that (debatably) almost ended your tribe...you think you'd learn (Nuada the High King loses his arm in battle...and has to leave the position, which is then offered to a beautiful (but tainted) successor.....its been a huge pet peeve of just stupidity).<br /> To be a warrior species, who is all about the grand sacrifice, but man, if you lost an arm or something to save Gaia...you better die too because you come back seen as unfit to hold any leadership position.....given the bulk of Garou culture and their views on battle scars its just SO CONTRARY TO IT</div> </div> </div> </div>I also find it interesting that Furies get males to be more equal and the Bitten all have to be adults. But something based on one myth and bad research? Oh, let the child abuse and ableism continue!<br /> <br /> I kinda can see it from a Fae perspective (Balor and all), but given the ties being severed, ehh. I assume disabled children also didn't face this treatment among celtic groups in the middle ages and before?<br /> <br /> EDIT: <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> Actually, the First ed does state that some male metis are kept.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":110,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","user":"Ana Mizuki","date":". 03-01-2017, 05:11 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T04:04:38-08:00","id":1056565,"title":"","content":"So I have finished reading the book, it's got some good points (The artwork, bonegnawers are now blue collar and not hobos) some bad points (The separation of the nation into factions based on Tribe and not personal belief, Cyberdogs why?) and some weird stuff (The bitten and Suddenly Beast courts!).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T04:55:28-08:00","id":1056567,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056565#post1056565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I have finished reading the book, it's got some good points (The artwork, bonegnawers are now blue collar and not hobos) some bad points (The separation of the nation into factions based on Tribe and not personal belief, Cyberdogs why?) and some weird stuff (The bitten and Suddenly Beast courts!).</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, cyberdogs are in vogue now again? O.o<br /> <br /> The Bitten bother me a lot. It takes away the tragedy of being a garou and so stuck in that state, but also that being a garou is also destined. The fact that the only way to become garou before the Bitten was to skin 5 garou and then get REALLY good at rituals, and even then that resulted in taint, should tell you how much being a garou was not an easy thing. Bitten just take away that feeling, plus add the whole &quot;I was turned&quot; aspect that really isn't needed.<br /> <br /> Plus, the whole 'children cannot Change' thing is kind of negated by the fact that metis still exist and they still get abused. If you don't want children to get involved in garou matters, don't leave metis in or change how they are treated. Otherwise it comes across as a bit dishonest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T05:06:39-08:00","id":1056569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056567#post1056567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Plus, the whole 'children cannot Change' thing is kind of negated by the fact that metis still exist and they still get abused. If you don't want children to get involved in garou matters, don't leave metis in or change how they are treated. Otherwise it comes across as a bit dishonest.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you keep saying....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T05:13:08-08:00","id":1056572,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056569#post1056569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So you keep saying....</div> </div> </div> </div>The Fianna metis section is pretty clear about how they are treated, isn't it?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T05:28:38-08:00","id":1056581,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056572#post1056572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The Fianna metis section is pretty clear about how they are treated, isn't it?</div> </div> </div> </div>\u200bA tribe that's known for tradition treating it's Metis in the traditional fashion, who would have thunk......","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T05:42:31-08:00","id":1056588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056581#post1056581\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> \u200bA tribe that's known for tradition treating it's Metis in the traditional fashion, who would have thunk......</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure what your point is here. Metis are abused by some tribes in the Nation as children, hence why I think the Bitten not changing as children which can be taken as the writers wanting to avoid child abuse, rings a bit hollow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T06:56:42-08:00","id":1056615,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056538#post1056538\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of a funny statement given characters like Evan Heals the Past being long standing canon characters. It seems like the authors didn't want to exclude, &quot;playing a white person that finds out they had some tiny amount of indigenous people in them and wants to connect with that heritage,&quot; as something these Tribes deal with.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, Evan heal the past is the ultimate example of a special snowflake. Only surpassed slightly by Sam Heigh, but he has issues of his own aside from being a special snowflake. He is the one and only white wendigo who was chosen by wendigo himself to be part of the tribe, he is part of a pack without totem and with 2 packmates lacking any deedname to them. He is part of the super special legendary pack and he barely does anything of worth and cant shift properly, he is just there because he is the one and only wendigo.<br /> <br /> The only reason he wasnt the last of the last of the white howlers is because they were probably saving that one for the videogame.<br /> <br /> He isnt really the measuring stick for typical PCs, neither his pack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2179-lokiravenspeak","name":"LokiRavenSpeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T07:12:20-08:00","id":1056621,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056615#post1056615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> To be fair, Evan heal the past is the ultimate example of a special snowflake. Only surpassed slightly by Sam Heigh, but he has issues of his own aside from being a special snowflake. He is the one and only white wendigo who was chosen by wendigo himself to be part of the tribe, he is part of a pack without totem and with 2 packmates lacking any deedname to them. He is part of the super special legendary pack and he barely does anything of worth and cant shift properly, he is just there because he is the one and only wendigo.<br /> <br /> The only reason he wasnt the last of the last of the white howlers is because they were probably saving that one for the videogame.<br /> <br /> He isnt really the measuring stick for typical PCs, neither his pack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Evan Heals the Past can die in a pit. I'm so sick of magical white saviors.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T08:14:48-08:00","id":1056638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056513#post1056513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They wouldn't NECESSARILY follow human cultural trends (and if that's not the route you'd want to take, it's perfectly valid), but I see a couple of reasons why it would make sense to take that route, and why it's a direction I personally prefer.<br /> <br /> From a lore perspective, it makes sense. These are creatures who live half in the world of man and half in the spiritual. Who they were before their first change informs who they become. The attitudes of their kinfolk and the other people they see in their daily lives influences their decisions, and the political and social attitudes of the mortal climate creates opportunities.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then they get broken down worse than boot camp and are faced with the hard reality that their beliefs have been extra-wrong. And the tribe isn't necessarily going to support them in this internal struggle, because they need to be on the page where they're giving proper chiminage to the caern's spirits and not wasting time tooling around with white nationalists.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In more meta terms, I like my games to be a reflection of the reality I know, and a way of exploring that reality in interesting ways. Especially in modern games, I look for concepts that reflect my lived reality, warts and all, and I think looking for those kinds of patterns is an inherently human thing, and a core virtue of storytelling in general. If there's a tribe of fiercely female warrior women, I see fertile ground of allegory for the feminist struggles I see in the groups I run in. When I see the Get, I see a reflection of military warrior culture and the reflectively hostile insularity of much of modern far right conservatism (and admittedly, my opinion is probably the outlier here, and I'm not expecting the writers to create a game tailored to my preferences). </div> </div> </div>Why would the Get be part of the American right? They're incredibly likely to cultivate their Rage high enough to scare off most humans that approach them. They live for war fought hard with hammers, axes, and claws, and venerate a wolf with jaws large enough to reach the heavens when they open, the enemy of the Northfolk's All-Father. By all rights, they should be recruiting any and all new blood from the steelier members of the SCA or from driven athletes from all walks of life.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> For me, at least, Werewolf is very much a game about the safety of the past: the threat of a mythical history that obfuscates the troubles that past represented, and the inability to achieve that in the face of an uncertain and frightening future. It's not the major theme for me (that would likely be the dual natured romance and dangers of radical ideology and the questions of moral righteousness when faced with an unbeatable threat), but it's prominent; and, as much as I abhor and pity the rising prominence of vaguely fascist nationalism, I think there's a stark metaphor in those people's apocalyptic view of the future, a future where they see their values, or religion, or racial identity, or whatever, threatened by existential genocide. </div> </div> </div>And, in turn, the Garou are so old that they, oddly enough, wouldn't buy into the human ideologies on account of their disdain for humanity. They have a mission that matters more. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In regards to the new writers skipping right over Revised, not gonna argue with you there. That sucks, and I'll be honest, I don't find a lot of these ideas, as presented, as very palatable. That said, it's been over a decade now. If the writers decided they wanted to undertake some rather major retcons for the sake of a bold new setting, I wouldn't be adverse to that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> But again, these changes don't indicate an edition that's going to appeal to me.<br /> <br /> I'm curious about your thoughts though. How do you perceive the Get? What's their hook for you? And how would you like to see them develop in 5e? It's been quite a few years, so there's a lot of possibilities for how they might have evolved. </div> </div> </div>Well, for starters, I wanted to see them have a multi-branched tribe like the Shadow Lords/Hakken, based on legends of monters that threaten to swallow celestial objects. Hilariously, this would involve taking one name from Forsaken, in a way (Rahu, from India), while there are also legends of such a wolf in China (Tiangou, oddly enough, the namesake of the Japanese Tengu). There are a number of other tribes currently presented as just European that could also deal with the same treatment; we're going Silver Fangs here and getting them spread out over the world, to get them to actually look old and well-traveled over the millennia.<br /> <br /> For the Get, like the Furies, what is important is anti-myth. The Revised tribebook had the Get presented as turning many bits of Northern European legendry on their head. For example, Fenris is not one of the progeny of Loki; instead, he arose more or less on his own and has been on a quest for personal growth and his image was conjured to convince Odin that he was surrounded by threats. Flat-out wrong by established myth, sure, but Werewolf is going to kick most of the sensibilities that humans are right about anything to the curb, so you might as well get myths and legends in on it, too.<br /> <br /> Generally, I think of them as more concerned with some personal endeavor than with a group one. The group isn't going to grow your prowess and might for you; you have to do it on your own. They're also very likely to spend more time on sojourns to accomplish this, with the weakness being that cultivating strength is something they take to be time-consuming and which tends to get them to lose track of subtle goings on more easily.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T08:20:02-08:00","id":1056642,"title":"","content":"The Appeal the Get have for me is they are a tribe that has made horrible mistakes in the past. They clawed first and asked questions later and discovered they fucked up. Thus the question is are the Get doomed to repeat their history or will they learn from their mistakes?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I write things.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3950-wonderandawe","name":"wonderandawe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3950_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T10:02:22-08:00","id":1056670,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LokiRavenSpeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056615#post1056615\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, Evan heal the past is the ultimate example of a special snowflake.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's really not the point though. The point is that the Tribal &quot;identities&quot; people seem to feel need to be preserved aren't something the original books actually cared that much about preserving. <br /> <br /> We can hate on Evan all we want (I do too, and I love the BNS Wendigo expansion as a much better approach to deal with the Tribe's issues by having them suddenly have an influx of northern Eurasian indigenous peoples who don't have sticks up their asses about the white colonization of the Americans to dilute the &quot;noble savage&quot; meh for a more complex look at the protection of such cultures in the face of assimilation), but if you tell someone to fuck off for wanting to play a white character that's a Wendigo or an Uktena, you're fighting the books for allowing such things. A player that wants to do the whole &quot;white guy connects to his great great great grandfather's tribe,&quot; you have very little stuff from the books to say, &quot;nope don't allow this because that's dumb.&quot; This is especially true for the Uktena who are repeatedly called out as being more mutlicultural and accepting of non-indigenous people into the Tribe.<br /> <br /> Saying fuck it to characters like Evan is us recognizing that the games don't.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wonderandawe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056642#post1056642\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Appeal the Get have for me is they are a tribe that has made horrible mistakes in the past. They clawed first and asked questions later and discovered they fucked up. Thus the question is are the Get doomed to repeat their history or will they learn from their mistakes?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think there's a problem here though, because that's all the Garou. This is the whole thematic point of elements like the War of Rage: the Garou tend have violence as a hammer and approach everything as a nail, in a stupid cycle of mistakes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T12:25:00-08:00","id":1056725,"title":"","content":"I get that white people claiming minuscule Native American heritage as either affected ethnic mystique or a privilege-deflector is a pretty pervasive and tiresome phenomenon. That being said is it any more correct to ignore the complex ancestral intermarrying that occurred during early American settlement, a meeting of cultures the history of which was often suppressed by the historiography of white supremacy? Is it any more correct to tell a white person with some amount of Native American heritage that exploring that heritage is off limits to them because they aren't pure enough, because they are irredeemably stained by their whiteness?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T17:10:37-08:00","id":1056864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056638#post1056638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Then they get broken down worse than boot camp and are faced with the hard reality that their beliefs have been extra-wrong. And the tribe isn't necessarily going to support them in this internal struggle, because they need to be on the page where they're giving proper chiminage to the caern's spirits and not wasting time tooling around with white nationalists.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Why would the Get be part of the American right? They're incredibly likely to cultivate their Rage high enough to scare off most humans that approach them. They live for war fought hard with hammers, axes, and claws, and venerate a wolf with jaws large enough to reach the heavens when they open, the enemy of the Northfolk's All-Father. By all rights, they should be recruiting any and all new blood from the steelier members of the SCA or from driven athletes from all walks of life.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> And, in turn, the Garou are so old that they, oddly enough, wouldn't buy into the human ideologies on account of their disdain for humanity. They have a mission that matters more.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Well, for starters, I wanted to see them have a multi-branched tribe like the Shadow Lords/Hakken, based on legends of monters that threaten to swallow celestial objects. Hilariously, this would involve taking one name from Forsaken, in a way (Rahu, from India), while there are also legends of such a wolf in China (Tiangou, oddly enough, the namesake of the Japanese Tengu). There are a number of other tribes currently presented as just European that could also deal with the same treatment; we're going Silver Fangs here and getting them spread out over the world, to get them to actually look old and well-traveled over the millennia.<br /> <br /> For the Get, like the Furies, what is important is anti-myth. The Revised tribebook had the Get presented as turning many bits of Northern European legendry on their head. For example, Fenris is not one of the progeny of Loki; instead, he arose more or less on his own and has been on a quest for personal growth and his image was conjured to convince Odin that he was surrounded by threats. Flat-out wrong by established myth, sure, but Werewolf is going to kick most of the sensibilities that humans are right about anything to the curb, so you might as well get myths and legends in on it, too.<br /> <br /> Generally, I think of them as more concerned with some personal endeavor than with a group one. The group isn't going to grow your prowess and might for you; you have to do it on your own. They're also very likely to spend more time on sojourns to accomplish this, with the weakness being that cultivating strength is something they take to be time-consuming and which tends to get them to lose track of subtle goings on more easily.</div> </div> </div> </div>Your take on the Get is an interesting one, and I'm sure far more faithful to the setting.<br /> <br /> I'd picture elements (granted, not all) of the Get that sometimes reflect and interact with the stalwart, insular, and sometimes out-and-out racist elements of military special forces, well armed and disciplined backwater survivalists, and hard right militant conservatives in America and Europe.<br /> <br /> I think we just have a difference in philosophy and preferences that really can't be breached. That said, yours is more in line with the books, and what I'm looking for probably isn't in line with WtA as written. It's been a long, long time since I've dug deeply into the game, but I need some point of meaningful intersection between the tribes and the mortal world to be compelled.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T17:13:12-08:00","id":1056868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056725#post1056725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get that white people claiming minuscule Native American heritage as either affected ethnic mystique or a privilege-deflector is a pretty pervasive and tiresome phenomenon. That being said is it any more correct to ignore the complex ancestral intermarrying that occurred during early American settlement, a meeting of cultures the history of which was often suppressed by the historiography of white supremacy? Is it any more correct to tell a white person with some amount of Native American heritage that exploring that heritage is off limits to them because they aren't pure enough, because they are irredeemably stained by their whiteness?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> That's between the people and their tribe, who usually have rules in place about who does and doesn't qualify for membership.<br /> <br /> But if you're looking to explore the heritage of your 1/64th Cherokee ancestry (and it's always Cherokee isn't it?), proving how you're a special snowflake probably takes precedence over your ethnic and cultural solidarity.<br /> <br /> All that said, the Wendigo and Uktena presented a worrying problem of how minorities are represented. Those sort of token ethnic splats were prevalent in Old World, and I'd hope the new edition takes efforts to steer away from them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","user":"dxanders","date":". 03-01-2017, 08:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T18:44:47-08:00","id":1056923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056868#post1056868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Those sort of token ethnic splats were prevalent in Old World, and I'd hope the new edition takes efforts to steer away from them.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's many WtA fans who'd like for them to stay.<br /> <br /> Werewolf: The Forsaken might be up your alley, however.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T18:49:03-08:00","id":1056926,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056923#post1056923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's many WtA fans who'd like for them to stay.<br /> <br /> Werewolf: The Forsaken might be up your alley, however.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forsaken didn't really strike me. That and Awakening are the two nWoD lines that never really clicked for me.<br /> <br /> I'm not against culturally specific splats. It's just they felt clumsily handled back in the day, probably in large part because they were written by middle class white American men.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8492-dxanders","name":"dxanders","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"378"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-01T22:45:18-08:00","id":1056994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056926#post1056926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Forsaken didn't really strike me. That and Awakening are the two nWoD lines that never really clicked for me.<br /> <br /> I'm not against culturally specific splats. It's just they felt clumsily handled back in the day, probably in large part because they were written by middle class white American men.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, yeah. Though the 1st ed isn't AS bad as you might expect, the first tribebooks made up for it by content (though CoG revised shall forever reign surpreme in badness). They had younger Fenrir as neo-nazi, Fianna as drunks, etc. Any non-general tribe was pretty badly written (minus Furies who actually are pretty cool in 1st ed).<br /> <br /> But for all that, I do think Uktena and Wendigo hold a very important role in WtA. They remind you that there are people out there who were hurt and you should not ignore that. Often they also serve as a way to notice when a game has some...issues with pocs as well. Banning them, the Striders and Stargazers is a very good indication that the game runner needs to check their views on race.<br /> <br /> And I'm glad that the writers grew up and wrote the tribes much more nuanced in later editions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T04:36:37-08:00","id":1057044,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>dxanders</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056926#post1056926\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">probably in large part because they were written by middle class white American men.</div> </div> </div> </div>...<br /> <br /> Okay. <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T05:00:16-08:00","id":1057051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056923#post1056923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's many WtA fans who'd like for them to stay.<br /> <br /> Werewolf: The Forsaken might be up your alley, however.</div> </div> </div> </div>Agreed this whole freaking out over it drives me nuts","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T13:00:26-08:00","id":1057204,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056923#post1056923\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> There's many WtA fans who'd like for them to stay.<br /> <br /> Werewolf: The Forsaken might be up your alley, however.</div> </div> </div> </div>Forsaken is only up your alley if you want a hunt over a war.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T13:44:29-08:00","id":1057229,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1056994#post1056994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But for all that, I do think Uktena and Wendigo hold a very important role in WtA. They remind you that there are people out there who were hurt and you should not ignore that.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always get frustrated in these sorts of discussion because this sorts of comments get really strange. The Black Furies and Bonegnawers are all about people that were hurt too.<br /> <br /> It always feels weird that people attach specific Tribes special importance towards themes that aren't really unique to those Tribes. It also gets odd that specific historically oppressed groups get multiple Tribes, while others are all just shoved into the general Tribes like the Gnawers or CoGs.<br /> <br /> The message of the game gets muddy with such uneven things. If I want to deal with indigenous peoples' history in the Americas, I have two Tribes specifically to that issue. If I want to do with in Europe, or most of Asia, there's no Tribe focused on that (at least unless you use the BNS Wendigo expansion); at best I have the Siberakh. The Silent Striders are extremely focused on Egypt and then the Rom, making all the North African non-Arab peoples left out in the cold in representation (so they end up mostly Gnawers). It's really easy to miss the &quot;remember all the people out there that have been trampled upon.&quot; when the games put a lot of focus on some peoples and virtually ignore others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Often they also serve as a way to notice when a game has some...issues with pocs as well. Banning them, the Striders and Stargazers is a very good indication that the game runner needs to check their views on race. </div> </div> </div>This feels... presumptive. That's actual part of my issue with the every ethnic focused Tribes. If I'm running a game set in Turkey, why shouldn't I ban Stargazers (a tiny Tribe in a place without a major south east Asian population), the Wendigo, and the Uktena from the game? It seems a pretty straightforward issue of verisimilitude one which Tribes would be in that part of the world rather than an issues I have with my views on race. With highly ethnically associated Tribes, there's going to be settings they don't make sense in because those ethnic groups aren't really prominent there.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And I'm glad that the writers grew up and wrote the tribes much more nuanced in later editions. </div> </div> </div>Definitely agree that I appreciate it; even with the stumbles that occurred.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1057051#post1057051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Agreed this whole freaking out over it drives me nuts</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh?<br /> <br /> Complaints about the &quot;ethnic&quot; Tribes in WtA has been going on for decades, because there's always been an odd tension between the more conceptual Tribes that might have some ethnic groups they're associated with, and Tribes that are extremely focused around specific ethnic groups which frequently got weird. The various camps on this and how/if to fix it are pretty old.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T14:05:21-08:00","id":1057241,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1057229#post1057229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I always get frustrated in these sorts of discussion because this sorts of comments get really strange. The Black Furies and Bonegnawers are all about people that were hurt too.<br /> <br /> It always feels weird that people attach specific Tribes special importance towards themes that aren't really unique to those Tribes. It also gets odd that specific historically oppressed groups get multiple Tribes, while others are all just shoved into the general Tribes like the Gnawers or CoGs.<br /> <br /> The message of the game gets muddy with such uneven things. If I want to deal with indigenous peoples' history in the Americas, I have two Tribes specifically to that issue. If I want to do with in Europe, or most of Asia, there's no Tribe focused on that (at least unless you use the BNS Wendigo expansion); at best I have the Siberakh. The Silent Striders are extremely focused on Egypt and then the Rom, making all the North African non-Arab peoples left out in the cold in representation (so they end up mostly Gnawers). It's really easy to miss the &quot;remember all the people out there that have been trampled upon.&quot; when the games put a lot of focus on some peoples and virtually ignore others.</div> </div> </div> </div>You are right in that, no doubt about it. The issue is more that often the WtA games that I've been into have been much better by giving attention to the Wendigo or Uktena cultures. Rather than a very solid white bread cast that populates most online games.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1057229#post1057229\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This feels... presumptive. That's actual part of my issue with the every ethnic focused Tribes. If I'm running a game set in Turkey, why shouldn't I ban Stargazers (a tiny Tribe in a place without a major south east Asian population), the Wendigo, and the Uktena from the game? It seems a pretty straightforward issue of verisimilitude one which Tribes would be in that part of the world rather than an issues I have with my views on race. With highly ethnically associated Tribes, there's going to be settings they don't make sense in because those ethnic groups aren't really prominent there.</div> </div> </div> </div>If a game is set in a certain area, then limiting the tribes is fine. But in more general games, there is no such reason why these tribes wouldn't be there. Especially if all the 'non-white' tribes are banned in a game set in an American city.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T17:41:30-08:00","id":1057357,"title":"","content":"I'll catch shit for this but whatever. I like tribes along ethnic and regional lines...I like the oppressive violent histories....I like that it makes people uncomfortable...I want to play in the world of darkness...not the world of let's make all the monsters friendly and kind and open minded and accepting of differences etc... If I wanted to walk on egg shells and plaster a fake smile and gasp whenever someone said something crude or offensive then I would go to my fucking boring PC office job and ask people how their weekend was when deep down I don't give a shit.<br /> <br /> Im drawn to WtA because it's tribal and horrible and closed minded and offensive and dangerous......I don't look at these books and disect them Into little polite tidbits. <br /> <br /> Everyone's got real world exerience I get that ( I guess)....but you wouldn't know It from the idealistic way I feel some of you view the actual world.<br /> <br /> I'm prepared to my lynching now","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T17:45:08-08:00","id":1057363,"title":"","content":"Also I get that the game is different for everyone and whatever floats your boat and all that shit , but sinc I'm gunna get burned at the stake I'm gunna go head and opine a little more. I get weirded out when people play WtA as an excuse to have werewolf mating fantasies.....that shit offends me....but by all means enjoy yo self","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T18:08:04-08:00","id":1057367,"title":"","content":"&quot; no way dude....that motherfucker across the street is garou I can smell it on him&quot;<br /> &quot; he's a wendigo&quot;<br /> &quot; bruh...when th e spirits taught me scent of true form they didn't say shit about detecting tribes&quot;<br /> &quot; dummy he's clearly a native and look at all that turquoise bullshit he has on&quot;<br /> &quot; that's super racist homie......I can't be in this pack anymore with you ignorant 1st edition cocksuckers&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T18:16:37-08:00","id":1057369,"title":"","content":"native across the street: &quot; i drank that fianna under the table.........I'm as good as in.....now I just gotta let my wendigo brothers down easy.......cause I can be fianna if I want too..wait....WTF are those Mexican bums staring at me for!?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T18:20:52-08:00","id":1057373,"title":"","content":"Lol calm down. <br /> <br /> I get the appeal of going back to 1st edition edge, it was written by early 20 something's who now probably look back on it and cringe a little. <br /> <br /> At the end of the day it's a book that you A) Don't have to buy if you don't like the content and B) Are free to change whatever you want to run the game.<br /> <br /> Frankly I think the whole By Night book is a tire fire and I regret buying it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","user":"BurritoMage","date":". 03-02-2017, 09:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T18:26:50-08:00","id":1057376,"title":"","content":"The rage burns deep","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T18:48:38-08:00","id":1057384,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1057357#post1057357\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'll catch shit for this but whatever.</div> </div> </div> </div>You generally catch less shit for things if you don't go in assuming everyone else is an asshole that's going to lynch you for having a dissenting opinion. Telling people that you don't think they're capable of taking what you said seriously and can't respond thoughtfully is more likely to get them to give you shit because you're giving them shit more than what you're actually saying.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I like tribes along ethnic and regional lines...I like the oppressive violent histories....I like that it makes people uncomfortable... </div> </div> </div>Most people here probably agree with you. The thing is that they want these things to be in-universe stuff, not out of universe stuff.<br /> <br /> A character that embraces their ethnic background, that brings the oppressive violent histories into the modern context of the game, and makes other characters uncomfortable? Cool!<br /> <br /> A Tribe that limits characters of an ethnic background into a specific narrative and attitude? Probably offensive out of universe, and also boring; thus making any offense pointless.<br /> <br /> The flat Wendigo characterization as a Tribe that's obsessed with being angry about European colonialism to the detriment of actually exploring modern indigenous cultural issues isn't fun because it's offensive to the actual struggles of real people, and it isn't fun because it's a dull narrative.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If I wanted to walk on egg shells and plaster a fake smile and gasp whenever someone said something crude or offensive then I would go to my fucking boring PC office job and ask people how their weekend was when deep down I don't give a shit. </div> </div> </div>I always find this sort of thing very hollow. Most people play with people that are their friends (or at least social groups they have a personal investment in). Not insulting your friends isn't &quot;walking on eggshells&quot; it's... being their friend. If you're constantly being an ass to your friends... how are they still your friends? Regulating your behavior to the social norms of your peers is natural behavior. We notice it in places like work because it's not a social unit we feel the same attachment to as friends or family, but we do it all the time anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1057363#post1057363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I get weirded out when people play WtA as an excuse to have werewolf mating fantasies.....that shit offends me....but by all means enjoy yo self</div> </div> </div> </div>Who the fuck cares?<br /> <br /> I mean seriously. If it's not your thing, and nobody's trying to make you participate, what does it matter if people get their strange sex shit on with a RPG?<br /> <br /> Go read some Chuck Tingle and get back to us when &quot;Homid Garou on wolf&quot; sex feels boringly normal.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>WISDOMINCHAINS</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1057367#post1057367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot; no way dude....that motherfucker across the street is garou I can smell it on him&quot;<br /> &quot; he's a wendigo&quot;<br /> &quot; bruh...when th e spirits taught me scent of true form they didn't say shit about detecting tribes&quot;<br /> &quot; dummy he's clearly a native and look at all that turquoise bullshit he has on&quot;<br /> &quot; that's super racist homie......I can't be in this pack anymore with you ignorant 1st edition cocksuckers&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Or rather:<br /> <br /> &quot;That's stupidly racist homie. I can't be in this pack anymore because you're so stupid there's know way we're not going to die when you get into a fight and keep clawing us instead of the enemy.&quot;<br /> <br /> Since this character is clearly really that stupid.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-02T18:57:29-08:00","id":1057392,"title":"","content":"Jesus Christ!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12902-wisdominchains","name":"WISDOMINCHAINS","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12902_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"139"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-03T00:34:12-08:00","id":1057487,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Wisdominchains, stop the threadcrapping. I'll cut you some slack since you are apparently a new forum u