ght</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1060928#post1060928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">At wolves and whiskey, heard that their were DEATH THREATS made because of the black furies accepting transvestites thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not the term you should be using, there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-10T17:47:44-08:00","id":1061087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1060928#post1060928\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I (who just heard about that there) thought that was an absurd reaction, but did, politely register my displeasure, it feels, a bit too preachy, and dillutes a core theme.</div> </div> </div> </div>What's preachy about a Tribe that seeks to protect those most disenfranchised by human social institutions being more inclusive of groups facing such social oppression?<br /> <br /> What's diluted thematically by the Black Furies accepting all women instead of just one narrow definition of woman (let alone why should the Tribe's themes be gender exclusionary at all)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T13:00:55-08:00","id":1061318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1061087#post1061087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What's preachy about a Tribe that seeks to protect those most disenfranchised by human social institutions being more inclusive of groups facing such social oppression?</div> </div> </div> </div>You mean the Children of Gaia and Bone Gnawers? Nothing at all.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> What's diluted thematically by the Black Furies accepting all women instead of just one narrow definition of woman </div> </div> </div>It's tricky. I'm on the side that, since werewolves grew up in human society, the younger ones would be more accepting, due to the new cultural trends. But that's not how it was before and in historical times, so I think that would an interesting tension between young and older members and progressive and traditionalist members (and you'd always have a fair ammounts of the latter ones).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (let alone why should the Tribe's themes be gender exclusionary at all)? </div> </div> </div>Why shouldn't? It's a plausible worldview, both historically and mystically to rally around.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T14:39:18-08:00","id":1061340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1061318#post1061318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You mean the Children of Gaia and Bone Gnawers?</div> </div> </div> </div>And the Uktena, and the Black Furies.<br /> <br /> I've spent plenty of time saying that I find the amount of overlap by the Tribes as being part of the problem with them in WtA. That doesn't actually address the point.<br /> <br /> The Black Furies are a Tribe that defends people from the inequities of patriarchal societies. How does it change the &quot;preachy&quot; status of this concept to have them be more inclusive in their ranks of people that suffer under the same systems they fight against when protecting people?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm on the side that, since werewolves grew up in human society, the younger ones would be more accepting, due to the new cultural trends. But that's not how it was before and in historical times, so I think that would an interesting tension between young and older members and progressive and traditionalist members (and you'd always have a fair ammounts of the latter ones). </div> </div> </div>Here's a big problem with this whole thing.<br /> <br /> I agree that it is thematically appropriate for the Garou of a Tribe to think that way.<br /> <br /> But who gets to be in a Tribe <b>does not work that way</b>. The Tribal Totems decide who can and can't be in the Tribe. That's why male Metis are in. Pegasus said so. Griffin rejects homids even if a Red Talon thinks rejecting homids is silly and tries to initiate ones that want to fight the Talons' fight. Wendigo said yes to Ethan Heals the Past even if most Wendigo Garou think that's bullshit, and they have to suck it up that Wendigo said yes to him anyway. The Silver Fangs can claim all they want that no Silver Fang would violate the Litany and produce a Metis child voluntarily, but Falcon still welcomes in Metis even if the Fangs would rather maintain the appearance to the contrary.<br /> <br /> We can't have, &quot;elder TERFs vs. modern third-wave inclusion feminists&quot; as a Tribal dynamic if Pegasus rejects transwomen outright. Either Pegasus rejects them, and the TERFs are &quot;right,&quot; or Pegasus accepts them, and how that's looked over the course of history regarding the individual Black Furies seeking to allow transwomen into their ranks is what's changed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Why shouldn't? It's a plausible worldview, both historically and mystically to rally around. </div> </div> </div>I'm sure <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar281_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"281\" data-vbnamecard=\"281\">atamajakki</a> can go into all the details on why this is actually not all that true.<br /> <br /> But basically, no, it isn't. The mentality that this reflects is extremely modern. It has minimal if any basis in the history or mystic traditions the Black Furies draw from.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T15:39:16-08:00","id":1061362,"title":"","content":"I spent an entire trainwreck of a thread arguing this point; I'm not terribly keen on doing it again. <br /> <br /> But Ancient Greek myth is rife with characters who were one gender and become another, one of the largest cults in the Greco-Roman world was that of Cybele/Magna Mater whose priesthood consisted of self-castrating men who lived as women, and if my memory serves Pegasus canonically was male and became female within Werewolf's own lore. I'm skpetical of any argument that suggests the Tribe defined solely by their respect for womanhood would ever turn away any woman, that any group so profoundly involved in matters of the spirit would be nearly as hung up on something so trivial as flesh determining what makes someone who they truly are. <br /> <br /> I see no argument for why the Black Furies should be transphobic outside of a desire to see transphobia in the setting, and that's a motivation I find profoundly suspect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T15:40:56-08:00","id":1061363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1061340#post1061340\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And the Uktena, and the Black Furies.<br /> <br /> I've spent plenty of time saying that I find the amount of overlap by the Tribes as being part of the problem with them in WtA. That doesn't actually address the point.<br /> <br /> The Black Furies are a Tribe that defends people from the inequities of patriarchal societies. How does it change the &quot;preachy&quot; status of this concept to have them be more inclusive in their ranks of people that suffer under the same systems they fight against when protecting people?</div> </div> </div> </div>The Children and the Gnawers doing it in general. Furies and Uktena are doing it in particular. They're focused on specific groups and that's okay to me., because groups could and are do work that way IRL.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Here's a big problem with this whole thing.<br /> <br /> I agree that it is thematically appropriate for the Garou of a Tribe to think that way.<br /> <br /> But who gets to be in a Tribe <b>does not work that way</b>. The Tribal Totems decide who can and can't be in the Tribe. That's why male Metis are in. Pegasus said so. Griffin rejects homids even if a Red Talon thinks rejecting homids is silly and tries to initiate ones that want to fight the Talons' fight. Wendigo said yes to Ethan Heals the Past even if most Wendigo Garou think that's bullshit, and they have to suck it up that Wendigo said yes to him anyway. The Silver Fangs can claim all they want that no Silver Fang would violate the Litany and produce a Metis child voluntarily, but Falcon still welcomes in Metis even if the Fangs would rather maintain the appearance to the contrary.<br /> <br /> We can't have, &quot;elder TERFs vs. modern third-wave inclusion feminists&quot; as a Tribal dynamic if Pegasus rejects transwomen outright. Either Pegasus rejects them, and the TERFs are &quot;right,&quot; or Pegasus accepts them, and how that's looked over the course of history regarding the individual Black Furies seeking to allow transwomen into their ranks is what's changed. </div> </div> </div>Ah, I see. Well, I think there's a room for a very picky totem, just as there's a room for a lupus-only totem, but it indeed takes away some possibilities for interesting conflicts within the tribe. However, it makes room for interesting conflicts between members of the tribe and their totem and bears the question: what if enough young members think otherwise? Would Pegasus change her way, after a point, thus creating a new situation and conflict between the aforementioned groups?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I'm sure <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar281_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"281\" data-vbnamecard=\"281\">atamajakki</a> can go into all the details on why this is actually not all that true.<br /> <br /> But basically, no, it isn't. The mentality that this reflects is extremely modern. It has minimal if any basis in the history or mystic traditions the Black Furies draw from. </div> </div> </div>Since, I'm interested in this, but it's not my primary field of knowledge, if you have serious arguments of why mystical groups didn't view womanhood in that way, or if you have papers or articles debunking the very existence of women-only groups(mystical or political) please share! I might add, that separated, individual cases aren't the norm, just like cases of women picking up weapons in historical times weren't the norm. Something can be true in general, despite the existence of differing individual examples","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T15:53:18-08:00","id":1061370,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1061362#post1061362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I spent an entire trainwreck of a thread arguing this point; I'm not terribly keen on doing it again.<br /> <br /> But Ancient Greek myth is rife with characters who were one gender and become another, one of the largest cults in the Greco-Roman world was that of Cybele/Magna Mater whose priesthood consisted of self-castrating men who lived as women, and if my memory serves Pegasus canonically was male and became female within Werewolf's own lore. I'm skpetical of any argument that suggests the Tribe defined solely by their respect for womanhood would ever turn away any woman, that any group so profoundly involved in matters of the spirit would be nearly as hung up on something so trivial as flesh determining what makes someone who they truly are.<br /> <br /> I see no argument for why the Black Furies should be transphobic outside of a desire to see transphobia in the setting, and that's a motivation I find profoundly suspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have been writing the same time.<br /> <br /> Interesting, thanks! For the record, I agree that because of the spiritual side of the thing and Pegasus' own transformation (that's a big point), I don't have any trouble Her accepting transwomen in the tribe. However, I think, individual members could have problems with it, just like <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar617_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"617\" data-vbnamecard=\"617\">Heavy Arms</a>' examples about Wendigo and Falcon and that's okay to me, as a story and setting element.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, I still think that accepting males is entirely different and not in line with the concept of the tribe and I agree it takes away from it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T19:00:42-08:00","id":1061408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1061362#post1061362\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I spent an entire trainwreck of a thread arguing this point; I'm not terribly keen on doing it again.<br /> <br /> But Ancient Greek myth is rife with characters who were one gender and become another, one of the largest cults in the Greco-Roman world was that of Cybele/Magna Mater whose priesthood consisted of self-castrating men who lived as women, and if my memory serves Pegasus canonically was male and became female within Werewolf's own lore. I'm skpetical of any argument that suggests the Tribe defined solely by their respect for womanhood would ever turn away any woman, that any group so profoundly involved in matters of the spirit would be nearly as hung up on something so trivial as flesh determining what makes someone who they truly are.<br /> <br /> I see no argument for why the Black Furies should be transphobic outside of a desire to see transphobia in the setting, and that's a motivation I find profoundly suspect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also, even Mage's Sisters of Hippolyta, who IIRC were in the past editions TERFs, loosened up their belts for their anniversary edition, so beings that are often ideologically in line with the Wyld and have a tribal code with the tenet &quot;Help the Helpless&quot; should probably be more accepting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T19:09:03-08:00","id":1061410,"title":"","content":"Ok I have to ask, what does &quot;IIRC&quot; mean?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T19:10:22-08:00","id":1061412,"title":"","content":"If I remember/recall correctly","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-11T20:16:42-08:00","id":1061422,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1061363#post1061363\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're focused on specific groups and that's okay to me., because groups could and are do work that way IRL.</div> </div> </div> </div>Being focused on helping a group doesn't inherently mean only members of that group can be members.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> However, it makes room for interesting conflicts between members of the tribe and their totem and bears the question: </div> </div> </div>Meh. Between the two &quot;interesting&quot; options here, I think enabling inter-generational conflicts in the Tribes is vastly more important to the tone of the game, and beneficial to actually playing the game, than Tribe-Totem conflict. The Tribal Totems are not generally active components of the majority of game-play. Every Garou will be impacted by inter-generational conflicts within the Tribe; even if that isn't the focus of a particular game. Exceedingly few Garou will ever actively interact with their Tribal Totem.<br /> <br /> And that's even before getting into cultural/political issues like increased representation and sensitivity towards minorities in the text.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Since, I'm interested in this, but it's not my primary field of knowledge, if you have serious arguments of why mystical groups didn't view womanhood in that way, or if you have papers or articles debunking the very existence of women-only groups(mystical or political) please share! </div> </div> </div>This is effectively asking me to prove a negative.<br /> <br /> But that aside, there's no evidence that the modern concept of sex and gender was constant throughout history.<br /> <br /> As well &quot;women only&quot; groups is as difficult as a concept to assert as &quot;this is not a norm.&quot; Women-only groups - and especially vagina only groups - are exceptions, not norms, and frequently part of larger organizations. Vestal virgins are an example of such, but they were part of the larger Roman state religion, etc. Single gender groups as an independent body (like a Garou Tribe) didn't exist because they can't continue on their own. They're always parts of larger social units that can produce members for them (aka they're Camps to a Tribe in WtA terms). <br /> <br /> You asserted a specific stance on history and mythology, but haven't done anything to actually back it up. It's generally considered good form to back up your point before demanding evidence from those challenging its validity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1061370#post1061370\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the other hand, I still think that accepting males is entirely different and not in line with the concept of the tribe and I agree it takes away from it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can you articulate how it &quot;takes away&quot; from the Tribe in a fashion that does not circularly rely on the Tribe having originally been defined as a Tribe of all women (esp. since there's already a large exception to that anyway)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T06:47:22-07:00","id":1061526,"title":"","content":"What really bothers me, still, is the treatment Red Talons got in the book. Because the tribe is almost completely seen as unplayable, psychopaths or just useless. So here was the writers' chance to change that and make the tribe more playable and fun for a wider audience.<br /> <br /> Instead, they took every single thing that was positive about the tribe and threw it in the bin. Worse, they literally had Red Talons willingly accept a torture focused camp that was somewhat of a secret society, openly start creating kill squads even in Africa where they actually have a better relationship with other fera, focus way WAY too much on dominance while avoiding the actual term, and take out the camp that could have actually been great as a more popular faction.<br /> <br /> I mean, Furies got updated, Gnawers got updated. But the tribe that needed it the most was downgraded to be even worse than it was in 1st edition. Was the focus of the changes just on 'positive' tribes?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T07:20:13-07:00","id":1061535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1061526#post1061526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">focus way WAY too much on dominance while avoiding the actual term</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you mean? I do not have the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5592-alonne","name":"Alonne","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5592_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T08:02:48-07:00","id":1061541,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Alonne</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1061535#post1061535\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> How do you mean? I do not have the book.</div> </div> </div> </div>Throwing around the term alpha left and right without concern for what the term means in the context of wild wolves (i.e. parents to a family unit, not who run Bartertown).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T18:46:00-07:00","id":1061686,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1061526#post1061526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Was the focus of the changes just on 'positive' tribes?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd wager it has a lot more to do with the popularity of the Tribes in the bigger LARP communities. Lupus and the Red Talons in particular tend to be poorly regarded in a lot of LARPs I've seen, and I wouldn't be surprised if that mentality went into making the Talons worse for playing in BNS WtA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T19:26:40-07:00","id":1061697,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1055874#post1055874\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Jobs are simply human jobs each auspice of a tribe can do in the human world. Given the role of kinfolk, and Rage, I rather dislike them being just randomly listed.<br /> <br /> The Bitten are kinfolk or Lost Cubs who, due to a bite from a garou, turn into garou.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> If that was true, that would be epically disappointing....can't even properly articulate how much that would bother me","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T19:39:00-07:00","id":1061701,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1061686#post1061686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd wager it has a lot more to do with the popularity of the Tribes in the bigger LARP communities. Lupus and the Red Talons in particular tend to be poorly regarded in a lot of LARPs I've seen, and I wouldn't be surprised if that mentality went into making the Talons worse for playing in BNS WtA.</div> </div> </div> </div>Might be, but that is then wasting valuable page space for a tribe made even worse. And that is pretty bad, considering they could have taken the time to change the tribe to be easier to play.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1179_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1179\" data-vbnamecard=\"1179\">CeltSPZ</a> - Yeah, it is true, sadly. I listed the jobs in this thread and they are rather...random.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T19:43:28-07:00","id":1061702,"title":"","content":"Oh, hit the wrong quote! I was actually trying to quote the line about tribe popularity impacting who got tune ups and who ended up worse...if LARP popularity was why i'd be epically disappointed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1179-celtspz","name":"CeltSPZ","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1179_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"835"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-12T19:50:35-07:00","id":1061703,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CeltSPZ</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1061702#post1061702\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, hit the wrong quote! I was actually trying to quote the line about tribe popularity impacting who got tune ups and who ended up worse...if LARP popularity was why i'd be epically disappointed</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, regardless, it is pretty bad. I haven't checked the Wendigo section well, but hopefully they got out luckier. Stargazer section is kinda ugh, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T09:54:20-07:00","id":1061862,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1061686#post1061686\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I'd wager it has a lot more to do with the popularity of the Tribes in the bigger LARP communities. Lupus and the Red Talons in particular tend to be poorly regarded in a lot of LARPs I've seen, and I wouldn't be surprised if that mentality went into making the Talons worse for playing in BNS WtA.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mine is only one perspective but in my experiences Red Talons have been one of the <i>more</i> popular tribes in LARP, to the point that they're usually restricted because more people want to play them than can necessarily really RP Lupus well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T18:15:44-07:00","id":1062109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1061862#post1061862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">...more people want to play them than can necessarily really RP Lupus well.</div> </div> </div> </div>Honestly, I find this to be the flip side of the same coin. The mentality that you have to RP &quot;so well&quot; to be allowed to play a Lupus (as if that's the only kind of Garou that can be very tough to RP well), is just a nice way of looking down on most Lupus characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T20:06:48-07:00","id":1062147,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Caitiff Primogen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1061862#post1061862\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mine is only one perspective but in my experiences Red Talons have been one of the <i>more</i> popular tribes in LARP, to the point that they're usually restricted because more people want to play them than can necessarily really RP Lupus well.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've seen the same thing but most of the players that take them is because of the gift/gnosis spread or because they a huge furries. (Not that there is anything wrong with that)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13009,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","user":"BurritoMage","date":". 03-13-2017, 11:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13009-burritomage","name":"BurritoMage","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13009_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"585"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T21:08:34-07:00","id":1062155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1062109#post1062109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Honestly, I find this to be the flip side of the same coin. The mentality that you have to RP &quot;so well&quot; to be allowed to play a Lupus (as if that's the only kind of Garou that can be very tough to RP well), is just a nice way of looking down on most Lupus characters.</div> </div> </div> </div>I can see what you're saying, but I would say the overall mentality is not as much an objection to Lupus specifically but objection to Lupus being portrayed poorly. Any Lupus concept tends to be met with greater scrutiny than a Homid concept, and as Red Talons are all Lupus that means that Red Talons as a Tribe tend to have more road blocks in the way of playing them. Though as I mentioned before this hasn't put any visible damper on their popularity.<br /> <br /> Regardless of the reasoning though I would say that you are correct in that the net effect is discouraging Lupus and Red Talon concepts in LARP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-13T21:13:36-07:00","id":1062156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BurritoMage</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1062147#post1062147\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I've seen the same thing but most of the players that take them is because of the gift/gnosis spread or because they a huge furries. (Not that there is anything wrong with that)</div> </div> </div> </div>Gifts and Gnosis definitely help. The main thing in the groups I've played in has been a desire to play what they perceived as the most hardline Tribe, as a lot of werewolf LARPers I've known tend to be really into Garou's various neoprimitive schticks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2507-caitiff-primogen","name":"Caitiff Primogen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2507_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1351"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T10:07:35-07:00","id":1072069,"title":"","content":"So, I read through Uktena, Wendigo and Ajaba sections. Ajaba too have begun to have a completely non-matriarchal culture, Wendigo have become more open minded but also more extreme (though I LOVE the new Weakness).<br /> <br /> Generally, what I am getting from these splat sections, is how the changes were made. If it was something that a socially aware person would want to be changed, it was. If it was something incorrect, making the tribe more fun to play, it wasn't. At times they even made things -worse-, such as with Red Talons.<br /> <br /> To me, the MET changes are very surface level, not really delving deep enough to actually fix issues that plagued the setting for a while.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T12:04:47-07:00","id":1072125,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1072069#post1072069\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, I read through Uktena, Wendigo and Ajaba sections. Ajaba too have begun to have a completely non-matriarchal culture.</div> </div> </div> </div>That reminds me of when they were first written.<br /> <br /> [/damning implications]","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T12:57:02-07:00","id":1072140,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1072125#post1072125\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That reminds me of when they were first written.<br /> <br /> [/damning implications]</div> </div> </div> </div>What really bothers me with it, is that it and the Valkyrie thing in addition of the Furies kinda confirms to me that they most likely just wanted an excuse for guys to play Furies/Valkyrie/ajaba.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T05:24:35-07:00","id":1073047,"title":"","content":"To add something to the Fury discussion: the Furies are in part about fighting the Patriarchy, in part about empowering women, in part about protecting the helpless and vindicating the oppressed and in part about a lot of other things, but that was never the whole of the Tribe.<br /> It could be clearer in the Core (go read the Revised Tribebook, it's awesome), but Furies are a mystical cult tied to living femininity as an aspect of Gaia. Living, not venerating. They don't need to accept males because they can understand women or because they speak up about women, they need to accept women who know what it is to be a woman. Yes, the Metis thing still makes little sense in this context but the source itself admits it.<br /> Furies do not hold egalitarian beliefs and are feminists only in the loosest sense. Males and females each have their distinct characteristics and purposes and one of these characteristics is an invitation to the clubhouse.<br /> <br /> So there's really no problem about accepting transexual or transvestites if Pegasus wills it (spirits do change, even Incarna and especially to reflect the beliefs of their worshipers) but whatever your definition of male is, the matter of including them in context is a little more complicated than &quot;they started accepting allies because 2017.&quot; It's a pretty heavy paradigm shift that should be properly addressed as such.<br /> <br /> The birth rate thing, by the way, is bullshit. Furies always birthed as many males as females. They just gave them up for adoption or, well, &quot;gave them up for adoption&quot;.<br /> <br /> Edited to add to the Revised comment: It almost seems like this incarnation of the Furies ignored the culture written up for them in Revised to build upon the material in the first Tribebook.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":29,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29-vidyaraja","user":"Vidyaraja","date":". 04-04-2017, 08:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/29-vidyaraja","name":"Vidyaraja","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar29_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T07:14:38-07:00","id":1073099,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vidyaraja</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1073047#post1073047\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To add something to the Fury discussion: the Furies are in part about fighting the Patriarchy, in part about empowering women, in part about protecting the helpless and vindicating the oppressed and in part about a lot of other things, but that was never the whole of the Tribe.<br /> It could be clearer in the Core (go read the Revised Tribebook, it's awesome), but Furies are a mystical cult tied to living femininity as an aspect of Gaia. Living, not venerating. They don't need to accept males because they can understand women or because they speak up about women, they need to accept women who know what it is to be a woman. Yes, the Metis thing still makes little sense in this context but the source itself admits it.<br /> Furies do not hold egalitarian beliefs and are feminists only in the loosest sense. Males and females each have their distinct characteristics and purposes and one of these characteristics is an invitation to the clubhouse.<br /> <br /> So there's really no problem about accepting transexual or transvestites if Pegasus wills it (spirits do change, even Incarna and especially to reflect the beliefs of their worshipers) but whatever your definition of male is, the matter of including them in context is a little more complicated than &quot;they started accepting allies because 2017.&quot; It's a pretty heavy paradigm shift that should be properly addressed as such.<br /> <br /> The birth rate thing, by the way, is bullshit. Furies always birthed as many males as females. They just gave them up for adoption or, well, &quot;gave them up for adoption&quot;.<br /> <br /> Edited to add to the Revised comment: It almost seems like this incarnation of the Furies ignored the culture written up for them in Revised to build upon the material in the first Tribebook.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, good point.<br /> <br /> The Valkyria among Fenrir allowing men is pretty bullshit. One day, a gay fenrir and his kin boyfriend wanted to be part of the camp (because?) and challenged for it and won. What that has to do with combating prejudices towards women in the tribe is up in the air.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-13T11:16:13-08:00","id":1267020,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> The Valkyria among Fenrir allowing men is pretty bullshit. One day, a gay fenrir and his kin boyfriend wanted to be part of the camp (because?) and challenged for it and won. What that has to do with combating prejudices towards women in the tribe is up in the air.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> I could not agree with you more on this point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2582-gangrel44","name":"Gangrel44","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2582_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"151"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T13:12:37-08:00","id":1267666,"title":"","content":"Is the BSN official canon or is the 20th Anniversary edition the last canon work?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T13:36:44-08:00","id":1267673,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1267666#post1267666\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is the BSN official canon or is the 20th Anniversary edition the last canon work?</div> </div> </div> </div>BNS is official canon for LARP, W20 for tabletop. The worry is NuWW will build off BNS for W5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-15T19:28:29-08:00","id":1267768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1072140#post1072140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What really bothers me with it, is that it and the Valkyrie thing in addition of the Furies kinda confirms to me that they most likely just wanted an excuse for guys to play Furies/Valkyrie/ajaba.</div> </div> </div> </div>These are exactly the kinds of things that make me frown.<br /> <br /> RPing an Ajaba male was always allowed, you just needed to realize that the leaders would always be females. Why is this supposed to be an issue, to the point of cancelling the matriarchy? It's like playing a drow but only as a rebel - a campaign that should be about 20 seconds long for your character and that steals all the charm and the social uniqueness from the game.<br /> And if you really don't like matriarchs, why are you playing as an Ajaba in the first place?<br /> <br /> Similar arguments could be done for Furies and Valkiries. Do a regular GoF, play a Metis, I can't understand what's to gain in depaupering the setting.<br /> Or, just let the male player cross-dress and play a female character; it's not like it's not allowed just because it's LARP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T03:37:27-08:00","id":1267794,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1073099#post1073099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Valkyria among Fenrir allowing men is pretty bullshit. One day, a gay fenrir and his kin boyfriend wanted to be part of the camp (because?) and challenged for it and won. What that has to do with combating prejudices towards women in the tribe is up in the air.</div> </div> </div> </div>The GoF are all pretty serious about physical challenges and challenging is a staplehold of Werewolf culture, so let's say that some master of the challenge decided to allow this kind of challenge. Even so, why after the Valkyrie lost there was no Rank 5 Valkyrie hero to re-challenge the gay garou (gayrou? XD) and kick him back and away again from the camp? I'd assume there would be quite a line of unhappy GoF waiting for the chance, and unless this guy is Golgol fangs-first he can't win every fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-16T08:49:00-08:00","id":1267858,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1267794#post1267794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The GoF are all pretty serious about physical challenges and challenging is a staplehold of Werewolf culture, so let's say that some master of the challenge decided to allow this kind of challenge. Even so, why after the Valkyrie lost there was no Rank 5 Valkyrie hero to re-challenge the gay garou (gayrou? XD) and kick him back and away again from the camp? I'd assume there would be quite a line of unhappy GoF waiting for the chance, and unless this guy is Golgol fangs-first he can't win every fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of reasoning in the writeups for the Garou in BNS make no bloody sense in context of everything that is presented in the RPG. That's the main reason why most of us balked when the writeups were posted...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-18T23:46:09-08:00","id":1268742,"title":"","content":"Is this latest edition being Kickstarted?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent-lax3-1.xx.fbcdn.net/hphotos-xfl1/v/t1.0-9/11999058_1477906402511404_6367649438608181692_n.jpg?oh=70d49fe91b2932b397dc24c5df2764ba&amp;oe=56A3338B\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1056-wolf-man","name":"Wolf-Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1056_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T02:58:08-08:00","id":1268772,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolf-Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1268742#post1268742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this latest edition being Kickstarted?</div> </div> </div> </div>W5th is being Kickstarted? I haven't heard ANYTHING about this, but then, I've been out of the loop and don't know anything about this &quot;nuWW&quot; (new White Wolf? This is a thing?) or what happened between OPP publishing W20 and the appearance of nuWW and BNS W:tA. I haven't read BNS W:tA yet, but from what alot of people are saying about it, it seems that alot of tribes are being reinterpreted/retconned into stuff that doesn't make sense to me (yet). I'll post more when I have a better idea of what's going on (and if people want to help explain here, that helps too).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T03:36:54-08:00","id":1268782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolf-Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1268742#post1268742\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this latest edition being Kickstarted?</div> </div> </div> </div>We have zero idea. Any plans for 5th books that aren't already in process (the three done by nWW already, and a few Onyx Path is doing for V5 including Chicago) are completely up in the air with the shake ups at Paradox.<br /> <br /> If Paradox operates more like CCP from here on out, and Onyx Path is their go to license partner for 5th books, then we'll probably see Kickstarters for W5's major books... assuming Paradox even keeps to the 5th line after all this.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1268772#post1268772\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I haven't heard ANYTHING about this, but then, I've been out of the loop and don't know anything about this &quot;nuWW&quot; (new White Wolf? This is a thing?) or what happened between OPP publishing W20 and the appearance of nuWW and BNS W:tA.</div> </div> </div> </div>Simplest possible version?<br /> <br /> In 2011 CCP dumped most of the original WW folks because the WoD MMO was on its way to dying. During this period Onyx Path and By Night Studios were founded. Onyx Path had the licensing from CCP to produce TT versions of the WoD, CofD, and Exalted games. By Night Studios got the license to produce the LARP versions of the games.<br /> <br /> Onyx Path continued to produce the 20th lines for the various WoD game that started when the CCP owned original WW made V20. BNS followed suit with new editions of Mind's Eye Theater books for VtM and WtA; with their own vision of balancing nostalgia, collecting lots of material in one place, and fixing lore and mechanics.<br /> <br /> Paradox Interactive bought the rights for the White Wolf imprint from CCP in the later half of 2015, the license deals with Onyx Path and BNS are assumed to have stayed the same in scope at a minimum.<br /> <br /> Paradox decided to create an independent subsidiary called White Wolf Entertainment Aktiebolag (or WW A.B. for short, it's a Swedish label similar to LLC).<br /> <br /> This &quot;new&quot; White Wolf created a new edition of the games (which they numbered as 5th) to kick off an attempt to revitalize the WW brand as both a top tier RPG, and a transmedia property with video games, and movies or shows, and so on.<br /> <br /> nWW produced VtM 5th aka V5, and has gotten its first two supplements early pdfs out to pre-order customers.<br /> <br /> However after multiple PR missteps with preview materials, play test content, V5 core's release, and now the V5 sources books on the Camarilla and Anarchs, Paradox has decided to revoke nWW's independent status and take control the associate properties directly. As I noted above, we have zero idea why this means for W5 moving forward.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I haven't read BNS W:tA yet, but from what alot of people are saying about it, it seems that alot of tribes are being reinterpreted/retconned into stuff that doesn't make sense to me (yet). I'll post more when I have a better idea of what's going on (and if people want to help explain here, that helps too). </div> </div> </div>It's something of a mixed bag without having read the metaplot BNS introduced for their new version of WtA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T03:52:59-08:00","id":1268785,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1268782#post1268782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We have zero idea. Any plans for 5th books that aren't already in process (the three done by nWW already, and a few Onyx Path is doing for V5 including Chicago) are completely up in the air with the shake ups at Paradox.<br /> <br /> If Paradox operates more like CCP from here on out, and Onyx Path is their go to license partner for 5th books, then we'll probably see Kickstarters for W5's major books... assuming Paradox even keeps to the 5th line after all this.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I really don't see a point of making a new edition yet, but that is just me. If they recanonized Shattered Dreams and not repeat Changing Ways mess, 20th lines wouldn't be too bad.<br /> <br /> <br /> For the BNS changes, I don't mind some. Silver Fang inbred-trait being either physical OR mental is a welcome thing, given how hard mental illness is to play. Bone Gnawers being lower middle-class isn't bad, as it addresses the obvious 'lol lowest are bums' issue. It is when it is things like the Red Talons or the Fenrir, where such mess was not needed, that my issues lay in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T05:20:00-08:00","id":1268805,"title":"","content":"Well, there's plenty of point really. Yet is a bit strange as a qualifier. The 20th books have had almost as much time as 2e did, and more time than Revised had. On top of this the 20th books never did a major rules overhaul. So, most of the rules are running on an engine that hasn't gotten tuned up in almost 20 years.<br /> <br /> Even as someone that really, really didn't like V5, and has no idea how they're going to make W5 work on that engine (VtM diminishing the role of combat mechanically is all fine and dandy if you want to focus more on the social/political aspects of vampires, but the V5 combat system is woefully underdeveloped to sate most WtA players that expect some fun fight scenes in their games), I want a new edition. W5 by Paradox/WW dictated to Onyx Path probably isn't going to be that edition for me. but WtA could still use a major update.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T07:25:08-08:00","id":1268846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1268785#post1268785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the BNS changes, I don't mind some. Silver Fang inbred-trait being either physical OR mental is a welcome thing, given how hard mental illness is to play.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is actually a bad idea, since it's against the official TT background. Also, inbreeding does not work that way.<br /> The association between Fangs, inbreeding and mental illness is mostly slander, hearsay and propaganda circulating between other tribes. The Silver Fangs do suffer from madness but that's caused by a curse from Luna, as explained in the Silver Fangs tribebook, and it only affects the kings of the tribe - it never activates on regular garou.<br /> <br /> Physical deformities or mental derangements are something that should be mandatory for Metis, not the Fangs. They could put some rule to make Silver Fangs more prone to Harano but that's it, as far as the setting goes. Requiring a generic mental illness is bs. =p","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","user":"Maris Streck","date":". 11-19-2018, 10:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T13:57:49-08:00","id":1268976,"title":"","content":"I'm generally against the Tribal Weakness as a whole. The Silver Fang one is particularly bleh because all the reasons Maris went over combined with the already overly modern European concepts of nobility and royalty in a Tribe that has an Indian sub-continental House, and a Middle Eastern based House. The Revised retcon to it being a curse is better, but it's better as flavor, not basic character traits.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T15:00:52-08:00","id":1268997,"title":"","content":"But in fact it doesn't affects the normal characters anymore, it strikes only seven Silver Fangs in the world - the kings of the houses. Six, actually, since Albrecht is probably going to be immune or die before it strikes (because of the Silver Crown and Falcon's blessing).<br /> Saying that every Fang needs to have a mental or physical illness is just like asking each Wendigo to regularly eat human hearts or each Uktena to have a dark pact with a bane. Picking a malignant rumor and making it a tribal weakness (with physical aspects, too) for a tribe that never had that kind of problem feels just cheap, and copying a breed trait to use it as a tribe one feels just poor game designing.<br /> <br /> The whole reason feels wrong: &quot;Let's give them physical deformities too because mentals are too hard to rp&quot;. What's next, physical deformities for Malkavians? =P<br /> I can't understand why BNS always feels the need to alterate the setting so much... just don't call it WtA.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T15:45:43-08:00","id":1269008,"title":"","content":"Honestly I'd make the Silver Fang weakness they lose an additional point of renown anytime they lose renown because more is expected of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T16:22:38-08:00","id":1269013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1269008#post1269008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I'd make the Silver Fang weakness they lose an additional point of renown anytime they lose renown because more is expected of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>But isn't that the same weakness as the Shadow Lords? Not saying if this is a good or bad idea, it just seems redundant for two tribes to have the same weakness.<br /> <br /> As for BNS metaplot, I'll look more into it soon, but I expect I'm going to have some serious issues with it if the vehemence of several posters here on this thread is any indication. The Bitten thing in particular (is that really a Garou version of the Ratkin Birthing Plague?) strikes me as especially ludicrous. Radical retcons to the established lore should only be done <i>if they make sense</i>, not just for adding more bells and whistles to a new edition in order to make it appeal to a wider audience.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/835/7xu8.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/546/wpur.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><br /> <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/folderview?id=0By9UuUWWH6CiMVlhWHMwNWcyaG8&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Complete Garou Gifts List, Fera Gifts List, Garou Totems List and other assorted OPP/White Wolf goodies</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2710-su-tehp","name":"Su-tehp","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2710_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"532"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T17:59:45-08:00","id":1269043,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1269008#post1269008\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly I'd make the Silver Fang weakness they lose an additional point of renown anytime they lose renown because more is expected of them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Getting pretty tangential:<br /> <br /> I've been mulling over ways to adjust how Renown works, and one of my ideas was that instead of 10 temporary Renown = 1 Permanent Renown, have how many temp. Renown you need be variable, with things like Rank and Pure Breed increasing how many temp Renown before you can increase because people expect more from you to care about your latest deeds.<br /> <br /> It's not a Silver Fang weakness directly, but their requirement to have Pure Breed 3 would basically have a similar impact without having to add another variable when figuring out rewards.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1269013#post1269013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for BNS metaplot, I'll look more into it soon, but I expect I'm going to have some serious issues with it if the vehemence of several posters here on this thread is any indication. The Bitten thing in particular (is that really a Garou version of the Ratkin Birthing Plague?) strikes me as especially ludicrous. Radical retcons to the established lore should only be done <i>if they make sense</i>, not just for adding more bells and whistles to a new edition in order to make it appeal to a wider audience.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah... like I said, it's a mixed bag. Some of it does work even if it' not what some of us like/would have done. Plenty is completely inane,","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T18:24:56-08:00","id":1269051,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1269013#post1269013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But isn't that the same weakness as the Shadow Lords? Not saying if this is a good or bad idea, it just seems redundant for two tribes to have the same weakness.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am thinking of it less as they are punished and more there are higher standards for the SIlver Fangs than others. Just like Red Talons and Glasswalkers basically have the same (Use Caerns, and hunt) flaw.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for BNS metaplot, I'll look more into it soon, but I expect I'm going to have some serious issues with it if the vehemence of several posters here on this thread is any indication. The Bitten thing in particular (is that really a Garou version of the Ratkin Birthing Plague?) strikes me as especially ludicrous. Radical retcons to the established lore should only be done <i>if they make sense</i>, not just for adding more bells and whistles to a new edition in order to make it appeal to a wider audience. </div> </div> </div>From what I remember part of the metaplot is that Garou can't be born anymore but those who WOULD have been garou can become garou through the bite and anyone else dies.. so plot basically gives Garou the birthing plague.. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T23:11:26-08:00","id":1269132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Su-tehp</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1269013#post1269013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for BNS metaplot, I'll look more into it soon, but I expect I'm going to have some serious issues with it if the vehemence of several posters here on this thread is any indication. The Bitten thing in particular (is that really a Garou version of the Ratkin Birthing Plague?) strikes me as especially ludicrous. Radical retcons to the established lore should only be done <i>if they make sense</i>, not just for adding more bells and whistles to a new edition in order to make it appeal to a wider audience.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't like the &quot;bitten&quot; part either. I get that some people might like it but I feel that it takes away the importance of kinfolk families.<br /> Changing the background to adapt it to some player's personal taste is also usually a poor choice as far as we're talking about RPGs. Every group can have their own house rules, of course, but should I start LARPing WtA I'd surely ask for a setting faithful to the tabletop version, and the fact that such a version does not exists means betraying some legitimate expectations.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I've been mulling over ways to adjust how Renown works, and one of my ideas was that instead of 10 temporary Renown = 1 Permanent Renown, have how many temp. Renown you need be variable, with things like Rank and Pure Breed increasing how many temp Renown before you can increase because people expect more from you to care about your latest deeds. </div> </div> </div>It's not half bad. I usually HR that higher pure breed means that you lose more renown then you should but asking for more to level up might be better (or just combinable), How much more renown do you ask? 2 for each PB dot?<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-19T23:21:06-08:00","id":1269135,"title":"","content":"Edit: This is in response to Lian<br /> <br /> That is... extremely inaccurate.<br /> <br /> In the BNS metaplot Garou and kin birth rates are increasing. The BNS metaplot says the dying of the Garou via breeding was actually a Wyrm attack that went unnoticed, but the war with Storm Eater pulled the banes responsible away to join in what was supposed to be the final battle. Thus the Garou and kin are flourishing without the Wyrm actively keeping their numbers down by decreasing their birth rates. It's also a potential cause of the Bitten (releasing all that energy into the system and such).<br /> <br /> Not defending these choices, but that's how the game is presented.<br /> <br /> -----------<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1269132#post1269132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like the &quot;bitten&quot; part either. I get that some people might like it but I feel that it takes away the importance of kinfolk families.</div> </div> </div> </div>Remember that the Bitten are basically Metis. They're sterile and can't Bite new Bitten either. So kin families and such are still pretty important.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's not half bad. I usually HR that higher pure breed means that you lose more renown then you should but asking for more to level up might be better (or just combinable), How much more renown do you ask? 2 for each PB dot?<br /> </div> </div> </div>Never settled on a final number because I got distracted by other things. It's a more complete overhaul because I don't like the way the sample rewards tend to play out and such. So keeping in mind lower temporary gains per event and less little details, as well as having boasting at Moots increase temp. Renown, I was looking at something like:<br /> <br /> Base + Rank + Pure Breed + Sept Standing - Position.<br /> <br /> The Base is something I haven't quite put numbers to but probably 4-6 points divided between each category based on Auspice. So Ahrouns would have a higher Glory Base than Wisdom or Honor because it takes more killing Wyrm for them to up their Renown than other Auspices. Etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 11-20-2018, 02:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T12:49:36-08:00","id":1269316,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1268846#post1268846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is actually a bad idea, since it's against the official TT background.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok here's the thing:<br /> <br /> From what I can gather, BNS's take on WtA was NOT designed with the intent of hooking in tabletop fans.<br /> <br /> That as is, much of WtA's setting and mechanics were unsuited for a LARP environment. That LARP games tend to lean more towards faction politicking. Something that's more readily apparent in Vampire and Changeling, but not in Werewolf. I guess they felt like moot politicking wasn't an interesting enough hook into a LARP. Which means making mechanical and setting changes to accommodate the new medium. It was purely just for making sure Werewolf worked in a LARP environment and that's it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-20T13:59:58-08:00","id":1269344,"title":"","content":"I think that's a fair point about a lot of stuff in the BNS WtA book... but I'm not sure how it applies well to the Silver Fang weakness. Giving the whole Tribe the need to pick a 'quirk' at creation doesn't have anything to do with making the game more LARP friendly. It certainly doesn't do anything to help make the game more political.<br /> <br /> Edit:<br /> <br /> To expand on this, the change in the Wendigo weakness from the weird seasonal thing to a straight up Frenzy modifier is clearly something for working better in the LARP on a few levels: it's simpler, and it work with most LARPs being real time and less frequent than TT play, so you don't have have half a weakness never come up because you only LARP twice a year a a big event, etc.<br /> <br /> Changing &quot;pick a derangment&quot; to &quot;use two dots of Flaws that don't provide you any benefit,&quot; doesn't seem to have any real purpose towards better LARP play.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","user":"Heavy Arms","date":". 11-20-2018, 05:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-21T20:10:30-08:00","id":1269729,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1269135#post1269135\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Edit: This is in response to Lian<br /> <br /> That is... extremely inaccurate.<br /> <br /> In the BNS metaplot Garou and kin birth rates are increasing. The BNS metaplot says the dying of the Garou via breeding was actually a Wyrm attack that went unnoticed, but the war with Storm Eater pulled the banes responsible away to join in what was supposed to be the final battle. Thus the Garou and kin are flourishing without the Wyrm actively keeping their numbers down by decreasing their birth rates. It's also a potential cause of the Bitten (releasing all that energy into the system and such).<br /> <br /> Not defending these choices, but that's how the game is presented.</div> </div> </div> </div>I Only read it once and noped out on seeing the Bitten but I remember something about the wyrm keeping people from properly changing who should have and that being a merit.. and the bitten really only being noticed because of the changes.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T20:37:25-08:00","id":1269978,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1268785#post1268785\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I really don't see a point of making a new edition yet, but that is just me. If they recanonized Shattered Dreams and not repeat Changing Ways mess, 20th lines wouldn't be too bad.</div> </div> </div> </div>To have Paradox-White Wolf get more control on it than OPP (May have) over Ww20 [Depending on Franchising arrangements]<br /> To have the system changes reflect across the board for the x5 range<br /> and finally, to set up the Werewolf world frame for the &quot;Transmedia&quot; part, whatever plans they have on that - TV/Movies/Games etc (The Pokie Machines they have for Vampire)<br /> <br /> For the Werewolf story and systems; by themselves it doesn't make sense to update so quickly to W5.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1268846#post1268846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This is actually a bad idea, since it's against the official TT background. Also, inbreeding does not work that way.<br /> The association between Fangs, inbreeding and mental illness is mostly slander, hearsay and propaganda circulating between other tribes. The Silver Fangs do suffer from madness but that's caused by a curse from Luna, as explained in the Silver Fangs tribebook, and it only affects the kings of the tribe - it never activates on regular garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds just like a Silver Fang, trying to talk their way out of the fact they keep breeding with their cousins.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1269051#post1269051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I remember part of the metaplot is that Garou can't be born anymore but those who WOULD have been garou can become garou through the bite and anyone else dies.. so plot basically gives Garou the birthing plague..</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah. It's not biting just anyone, it's biting someone that should have turned. If you try it on someone that wasn't going to turn; they will die painfully.<br /> It's an extension of a curse/plague from the Wyrm, not a new way to recruit.<br /> <br /> <b>P366 of Minds Eye Werewolf</b> &quot;They discovered that the majority of those Bitten suffered a horrific illness and died within a short time, but a precious few endured the horrific ordeal.....<br /> Potential werewolves became stuck in their development, just before their First Change. These individuals, known as Unborn, had existed previously, though in much fewer numbers. The Wyrm\u2019s efforts halted the transformation for a significant portion of the new generation of Cubs, creating a legion of Unborn. Nearly half a generation of werewolves was lost when the Garou Nation needed it the most. Extensive research eventually revealed the Wyrm\u2019s agents were actively denying these potential Garou their birthright\u2014preventing them from crossing the spiritual bridge and realizing their full capabilities as werewolves.&quot;<br /> <br /> The Black furies changing ratio of sex in child birth was another curse/plague from the Wyrm<br /> <br /> <b>Sidebar P 62 </b>&quot;The Metamorphic Plague visited upon the Black Furies during the Age of the Weaver birthed a new generation of children of both genders in equal numbers within this tribe. My mothers were among the first to keep children who were born male. I remember the pride on their faces during my Rite of Passage, when Pegasus looked into my heart and proclaimed the truth. Afterwards, they embraced me not just as their daughter, but a sister of the tribe.&quot;<br /> <br /> Personally, I think it's interesting, it gives an option for more character concepts for characters that don't have the same ties to the wolves as before. I like that it ties in some of the Mythology of Lycanthropy for the bitten.<br /> It also give something that's interesting; the Bitten can't offer the bite to the Unborn, but they're still Garou who can breed (Not Sterile from what I've found)<br /> Some Garou go through normally, so there's a divide with interesting complications.<br /> Kinfolk, who are really useful to Garou, have a lot wanting to try for the change, at a high risk of dying. Do you take the risk to get more Garou now, or not and have an upset Kinfolk, but more stable breeding stock in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T21:41:55-08:00","id":1270000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1269978#post1269978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Sidebar P 62 </b>&quot;The Metamorphic Plague visited upon the Black Furies during the Age of the Weaver birthed a new generation of children of both genders in equal numbers within this tribe. My mothers were among the first to keep children who were born male. I remember the pride on their faces during my Rite of Passage, when Pegasus looked into my heart and proclaimed the truth. Afterwards, they embraced me not just as their daughter, but a sister of the tribe.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>In this, I'd just have to ask; why'd they give a crap about it? Yes, more male children are born, great give the garou to other tribes. Like Furies have always done.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T21:44:01-08:00","id":1270001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1270000#post1270000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> In this, I'd just have to ask; why'd they give a crap about it? Yes, more male children are born, great give the garou to other tribes. Like Furies have always done.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly.........","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T22:09:51-08:00","id":1270005,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1270000#post1270000\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In this, I'd just have to ask; why'd they give a crap about it? Yes, more male children are born, great give the garou to other tribes. Like Furies have always done.</div> </div> </div> </div>The historian is &quot;Verity Argyris&quot; the implication is that she was assigned male at birth but accepted in to the tribe &quot;not just as their daughter, but a sister of the tribe.&quot; as a sign of accepting Transwomen now.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T22:43:02-08:00","id":1270013,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1270005#post1270005\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The historian is &quot;Verity Argyris&quot; the implication is that she was assigned male at birth but accepted in to the tribe &quot;not just as their daughter, but a sister of the tribe.&quot; as a sign of accepting Transwomen now.</div> </div> </div> </div>That would be fine. But the text in the tribe part clearly states that Furies are accepting cismen to their ranks. Not just Furies, either, Valkyria Camp in Get of Fenris accepts men and the Ajaba are now gender equal.<br /> <br /> I got NOTHING against Furies accepting transwomen, but I do find the trend of taking away female-only or female-led spaces rather unfortunate.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-22T23:30:20-08:00","id":1270021,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1269978#post1269978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For the Werewolf story and systems; by themselves it doesn't make sense to update so quickly to W5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering the list of things WtA needs better rules on? Yeah, they systems by themselves make sense to update to W5 &quot;so quickly.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That sounds just like a Silver Fang, trying to talk their way out of the fact they keep breeding with their cousins. </div> </div> </div>No, it's the Revised Silver Fang Tribebook retcon for the Tribal Weakness because the inbreeding justification is stupid out of game (that's not how inbreeding works, and royals inbreeding to the level of significant biological impact is a blip in the radar of history) and in universe (the Silver Fangs aren't actually any more inbred than any of the other Tribes that put a focus on Pure Breed and maintaining bloodlines like the Fianna, Fenrir, Shadow Lords, and Wendigo, perhaps less so when you consider the Silver Fangs have a bigger breeding pool than a lot of the ethnic/location based Tribes do).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> (Not Sterile from what I've found) </div> </div> </div>BNS WtA pages: 35, 322 (most important as it's the Flaw to make your character one of the Bitten), and 369.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1270013#post1270013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got NOTHING against Furies accepting transwomen, but I do find the trend of taking away female-only or female-led spaces rather unfortunate.</div> </div> </div> </div>All of the female-led spaces still are. Black Fury males (remembering that there have always been males in the Tribe) can't raise above Adren in Rank and aren't allowed positions of increased authority.<br /> <br /> The Ajaba are not gender equal, they're just not longer purely matriarchal. Male Ajaba in positions of power are exceptions, and their society is still based in matriarchal traditions.<br /> <br /> The Valkyries camp accepts men now, but it's not stated how equally they're treated. Though considering that the male Get that forced the issue is explicitly gay, the point of the group as fighting the toxic masculinity that permeates mainstream Get culture isn't really harmed by taking in men that suffer under it as well, or allies seeking to aid the cause. Camps are, after all, social affiliations, not spaces in this context.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T00:23:17-08:00","id":1270036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1270013#post1270013\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I got NOTHING against Furies accepting transwomen, but I do find the trend of taking away female-only or female-led spaces rather unfortunate.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't like it. Unless those trans women had a proper total sex change (not surgery, something like an Umbral quest to persuade Eshtarra to alter the garou's body) I wouldn't let Pegasus accept them. I understand that they want to stay in line with the times but they were the Amazons, trans women feel out of place there.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T05:29:59-08:00","id":1270090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1270021#post1270021\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All of the female-led spaces still are. Black Fury males (remembering that there have always been males in the Tribe) can't raise above Adren in Rank and aren't allowed positions of increased authority.<br /> <br /> The Ajaba are not gender equal, they're just not longer purely matriarchal. Male Ajaba in positions of power are exceptions, and their society is still based in matriarchal traditions.<br /> <br /> The Valkyries camp accepts men now, but it's not stated how equally they're treated. Though considering that the male Get that forced the issue is explicitly gay, the point of the group as fighting the toxic masculinity that permeates mainstream Get culture isn't really harmed by taking in men that suffer under it as well, or allies seeking to aid the cause. Camps are, after all, social affiliations, not spaces in this context.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is the point of these, though, if they don't affect things? In a general sense, why note the ajaba no longer are purely matricial? Or that Valkyries have male members? Nevermind Furies accepting cismen who are not metis?<br /> <br /> I'm against these, because they feel meaningless or just outright take away from the tribe. With Furies, their gender-exclusion very much defined them and not in a bad way. Take it away and they generally seem just more Wyldy Children of Gaia/Bone Gnawers/Glass Walkers. Sure, to veteran players there is a difference, but purely concept wise it just doesn't fit.<br /> <br /> With transwomen, the matter is different, because changing gender or physical sex is seen as very spiritual and boundary breakingin itself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ana-mizuki.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My gallery.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/110-ana-mizuki","name":"Ana Mizuki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar110_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2484"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T07:19:45-08:00","id":1270107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1270036#post1270036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't like it. Unless those trans women had a proper total sex change (not surgery, something like an Umbral quest to persuade Eshtarra to alter the garou's body) I wouldn't let Pegasus accept them. I understand that they want to stay in line with the times but they were the Amazons, trans women feel out of place there.</div> </div> </div> </div>As other posters have detailed many times in the past? The ancient Greeks especially for European cultures had a level of concept approaching modern gender; that gender was not your biological parts.<br /> <br /> Also... Pegasus started as a male spirit. So... the idea that Pegasus would be this picky about transwomen doesn't really make sense because Pegasus is the spirit that decides what is and isn't an acceptable Black Fury.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ana Mizuki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1270090#post1270090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the point of these, though, if they don't affect things?</div> </div> </div> </div>1) They do affect things, they just don't eliminate that these are female-led groups as asserted before.<br /> <br /> 2) They reinforce the BNS metaplot where all of these groups have been reduced in number by a huge extent, meaning a lot of their exclusionary attitudes fell to pure necessity and a new generation that's more inclusive. The BNS metaplot had the Gaian forces reduced to a tiny fraction of already small numbers during the battles with the Black Crusade and Storm Eater. They literally need every Garou they can get their hands on (also why the Bitten found acceptance despite some resistance, they just need the numbers too badly). Rejecting male born Black Furies from being raised as Black Furies and giving them a chance to prove themselves allies to their mothers, sisters, and daughters in the eyes of Pegasus is now a direct risk to the survival of the Tribe because that would leave too few Garou Black Furies around to do anything. If the Ajaba didn't let more males into positions of leadership... they'd be empty because there aren't enough proven females to go around any more. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> With Furies, their gender-exclusion very much defined them and not in a bad way. </div> </div> </div>Except it never defined them because they weren't truly exclusionary, and it is kind of a bad way because it's dumb to kick the men out of your Tribe (since that means reducing your breeding capabilities) just to assert a matriarchal society. Matriarchal societies have men. Patriarchal societies have women. If the Black Furies' matriarch is so fragile that allowing male non-Metis Garou in while denying them equal rights (since they already had male Metis and male kin in) destroys their concept as a matriarchal society... it so poorly constructed it wasn't coherent in the first place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T11:57:16-08:00","id":1270159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1269978#post1269978\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <b>Sidebar P 62 </b>&quot;The Metamorphic Plague visited upon the Black Furies during the Age of the Weaver birthed a new generation of children of both genders in equal numbers within this tribe. My mothers were among the first to keep children who were born male. I remember the pride on their faces during my Rite of Passage, when Pegasus looked into my heart and proclaimed the truth. Afterwards, they embraced me not just as their daughter, but a sister of the tribe.&quot;<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>was this ever thing? I don't remember the Furies being magically less likely to have male children.. they just gave them away.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1270036#post1270036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't like it. Unless those trans women had a proper total sex change (not surgery, something like an Umbral quest to persuade Eshtarra to alter the garou's body) I wouldn't let Pegasus accept them. I understand that they want to stay in line with the times but they were the Amazons, trans women feel out of place there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Since the Amazons are fictional its hard to tell, BUT many less patriarchal societies seemed to be much more accepting of nonbinary gender roles","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T12:43:37-08:00","id":1270180,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1270159#post1270159\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> was this ever thing? I don't remember the Furies being magically less likely to have male children.. they just gave them away.</div> </div> </div> </div>No it wasn't....which is just another in the long list of nonsense BNS has inflicted on WtA in order that LARPers can have even more special-snowflake characters....the days of every Camarilla LARP being composed of 50% Lasombra Antitribu and every Werewolf LARP choking on the numbers of inexplicable White Howlers are certainly not over.<br /> <br /> Pegasus judges acceptability and it is based on whether or not the individual Garou is spiritually female and dedicated to protect the Wyld and enforce Pegasus' edicts on humanity....so transfolk were always ok, cubs were always given to other tribes ( from the Middle Ages onwards) and there were always equal numbers of both physical sexes born to Furies and Fury kinfolk.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T16:05:16-08:00","id":1270214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1270107#post1270107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also... Pegasus started as a male spirit. So... the idea that Pegasus would be this picky about transwomen doesn't really make sense because Pegasus is the spirit that decides what is and isn't an acceptable Black Fury.</div> </div> </div> </div>IIRC Pegasus has a couple of canons in WW and no one was actually found definitive. In Umbra Revised it's portrayed as a female and lover of Bellerophon which became spiteful of men after the hero became a tyrant, but I seem to recall that there was a source that defined it as a male which decided to protect women after seeing Bellerophon's behaviour (no romance between the two in this version).<br /> <br /> Thing is that there is no raw saying the spirit shifted his form and changed sex - even assuming it's described differently in two different sources that's simply to be intended as two different forms of the myth.<br /> <br /> I also said that makes sense for Pegasus to accept trans women - hell, she might even offer to make the change herself (should the garou show herself worthy enough). I simply don't think it makes sense to accept them as long as they still are polluted with manhood, but that's just my take.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As other posters have detailed many times in the past? The ancient Greeks especially for European cultures had a level of concept approaching modern gender; that gender was not your biological parts. </div> </div> </div>As far as I recall, ancient greece was quite open and tolerant about homosexual relationships but it still was a place where the women couldn't vote, do politics or enlist in the army. I recall no parity in any of the epic literature or the myths, no mention in their whole written culture about women taking on man-reserved roles because they felt to be men inside and no mention of Amazons with a male body. Women were often portrayed as strong, loyal and determinate characters (Penelope, Arianna, Circe... Aristophanes wrote an entire comedy about all of the women in Athens going on a sex strike to strong-arm their husbands into voting as they wanted), but never in the shades of a gender theory or as if they could break out of their social role.<br /> <br /> I can't remember a single classical source portraying ancient Greece as a gender-fluid society.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the days of every Camarilla LARP being composed of 50% Lasombra Antitribu and every Werewolf LARP choking on the numbers of inexplicable White Howlers are certainly not over. </div> </div> </div>In my last Vampire TT game there was this player that couldn't shut up about wanting to play a Lasombra Antitribu. Luckily the ST didn't allow it, but still - it's a CAMARILLA campaign, just get over it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":13673,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","user":"Maris Streck","date":". 11-24-2018, 08:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-23T19:52:51-08:00","id":1270253,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1270180#post1270180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No it wasn't....which is just another in the long list of nonsense BNS has inflicted on WtA in order that LARPers can have even more special-snowflake characters....the days of every Camarilla LARP being composed of 50% Lasombra Antitribu and every Werewolf LARP choking on the numbers of inexplicable White Howlers are certainly not over.<br /> <br /> Pegasus judges acceptability and it is based on whether or not the individual Garou is spiritually female and dedicated to protect the Wyld and enforce Pegasus' edicts on humanity....so transfolk were always ok, cubs were always given to other tribes ( from the Middle Ages onwards) and there were always equal numbers of both physical sexes born to Furies and Fury kinfolk.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think its funny. Tabletop more readily supports Special snowflake setups and let they always say its &quot;larpers&quot; who are the ones who want it. A game that's A LAT cotorie in a Cam game.. is pretty damned easy to do in TT.. Larp is where &quot;the pcs are the only vampires in the City&quot; where it gets weird.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T17:11:55-08:00","id":1270722,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Damian May</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1270180#post1270180\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> No it wasn't....which is just another in the long list of nonsense BNS has inflicted on WtA in order that LARPers can have even more special-snowflake characters....the days of every Camarilla LARP being composed of 50% Lasombra Antitribu and every Werewolf LARP choking on the numbers of inexplicable White Howlers are certainly not over.</div> </div> </div> </div>If a Larp was half full of Lasombra Antitrubu or White Howlers, that's a problem with the Storytelling team accepting it, not the system for allowing it. Just because you CAN do it, doesn't mean it should be done. Would a Tabletop ST let everyone have true faith because the rules let it? No.<br /> <br /> That being said, I think that Larps need to allow characters to have more of a &quot;Special Snowflake&quot; characters (Though I hate the F-ing term) than a tabletop.<br /> You have 20% of your players in a TT who are Brujah (1 in 5) and they can be an individual due to the time an ST has to dedicate to the back story and personal life. If you have 20% of your players in a 50 person Larp as Brujah (10) they you want &quot;Snowflake&quot; capacity for them to feel special. Have weird Clan options because it opens up having PCs that are differentiated more easily.<br /> I don't care about having a single Nagaraja or Kiasd in a city, I'd do it for a large city in a TT, why can't a PC Fill that niche in a LARP.<br /> <br /> One thing I really, really like about BNS MET is the clan rarity merits, you have players spending their merit allocation to be this special. So they weigh it up more, and people <i>tend</i> not to do it if the concept fits as well with a more common clan. But if they really really want to do it; they will.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T18:14:53-08:00","id":1270726,"title":"","content":"I wasn't saying it was specific to LARP but we are discussing the changes to Tabletop setting material that the makers of the LARP rules made and why on earth they may have done such silly things....so I gave a personally observed reason as to why they may have made such changes...cos I honestly can't think of a good reason for the vast majority of them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/479-damian-may","name":"Damian May","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar479_1.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1199"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-11-25T19:06:11-08:00","id":1270737,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1270722#post1270722\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If a Larp was half full of Lasombra Antitrubu or White Howlers, that's a problem with the Storytelling team accepting it, not the system for allowing it. Just because you CAN do it, doesn't mean it should be done. Would a Tabletop ST let everyone have true faith because the rules let it? No.<br /> <br /> That being said, I think that Larps need to allow characters to have more of a &quot;Special Snowflake&quot; characters (Though I hate the F-ing term) than a tabletop.<br /> You have 20% of your players in a TT who are Brujah (1 in 5) and they can be an individual due to the time an ST has to dedicate to the back story and personal life. If you have 20% of your players in a 50 person Larp as Brujah (10) they you want &quot;Snowflake&quot; capacity for them to feel special. Have weird Clan options because it opens up having PCs that are differentiated more easily.<br /> I don't care about having a single Nagaraja or Kiasd in a city, I'd do it for a large city in a TT, why can't a PC Fill that niche in a LARP.<br /> <br /> One thing I really, really like about BNS MET is the clan rarity merits, you have players spending their merit allocation to be this special. So they weigh it up more, and people <i>tend</i> not to do it if the concept fits as well with a more common clan. But if they really really want to do it; they will.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> I think its the other way around. I can have a perfectly average city where the coterie is all LATs or sabbat Infitrators or whatever because they don't represent the majority of characters in existence. Larp goes the other way there are far fewer Npcs per pc. (Though a camarilla larp where everyone is secretly sabbat and they don't know it would be hilarious)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T14:08:12-08:00","id":1281369,"title":"","content":"Speaking as a Native on the topic of the Native Garou, their inclusion was what made me buy the book when I came across it on the shelf of a used book store back in the early 00s (aside from werewolves being my favorite classic monster). Despite their execution, I personally felt included in a Fantasy/supernatural fictional setting for once without us being solely a shitty Fantasy counterpart culture of tragic savages and/or a source of exotic wisdom, etc. I also liked how they were a fully functional part of Garou society instead of being outliers like their counterparts in Wraith or Changeling. Are there still severe issues with their execution? Yes. I could go on and on and on about it, but I don\u2019t have the time or the inclination to do so at this point.<br /> <br /> A big part of fixing them, and all the tribes that are heavily ethnic based, is there should have been a greater exploration of the purpose, origin, etc of what the tribes were before said ethnic groups formed and how the greater adoption of these human groups did to shape them. Because honestly, they tend to all feel really static compared to say Vampire clans, Traditions, the Legions, etc.<br /> <br /> Before Forsaken is mentioned as fixing this, it only went part of the way IMO. I like the greater purpose and mythical beginnings of their tribes being their origin point, and it really justifies how they remain these perpetual entities since Pangaea , unlike Apocalypse. However, for all my complaints about the static nature of the Garou tribes , the Urathra come off even more frozen, bland, and video game like. Nothing has changed since Father Wolf died thousands upon thousands of years ago, while in Apocalypse there\u2019s much more extensive history with the War of Rage, the Impergium, the fall of the White Howlers, Croatan, and Bunyip, and so forth. And again, given this \u201cuniversal\u201d nature of the Forsaken and the Pure, I don\u2019t feel included. It\u2019s very much Euro-American like all the NWoD games. Not to imply Forsaken sucks, because there\u2019s A LOT of material I love and prefer over Apocalypse, but it\u2019s far from this perfect replacement for the faults of Old Werewolf. Over the years, mixing up aspects of both games often fixes holes in the other, but this is another subject.<br /> <br /> In summery, each of the game lines committed the cardinal sins of trying to represent disenfranchised/minority groups. In the classic line, by trying to represent the uniqueness of other cultures, even European ones, they fell heavily into Euro-American stereotypes of these groups. While with the new games, they bleached it so much to be \u201cuniversal\u201d, they didn\u2019t realize they were basically falling back on the subconscious assumption that a neutral state of humanity is a Euro-American one. I\u2019m not trying to say that the writers are these horrible racists or alt-right jerks. I know they had nothing but the best intentions in mind for these games, but mistakes were made. Like Heavy Arms said, it\u2019s going to happen more often than not when people write about people, countries, and cultures they don\u2019t have much of or any personal contact with, especially when the internet was in its infancy.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> As for the original topic, I find the changes proposed for W5 terrible and detrimental to the game. These are not the changes WtA needs, and if OPP or some other entity pursues them, they will not get another cent from me. V5 was enough of an abomination, and the same goes for their terrible plans for M5.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":21481,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","user":"Onkwe","date":". 01-17-2019, 05:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T17:32:18-08:00","id":1281405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1281369#post1281369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A big part of fixing them, and all the tribes that are heavily ethnic based, is there should have been a greater exploration of the purpose, origin, etc of what the tribes were before said ethnic groups formed and how the greater adoption of these human groups did to shape them. Because honestly, they tend to all feel really static compared to say Vampire clans, Traditions, the Legions, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>A problem with all the tribes to an extent was how much they were derived from specific human ethnic groups/cultures as opposed to being their own thing separate from the culture of their kinfolk. That never made sense for metis and lupus, but even among homids not all homid members came from those cultures. Vikings were specific to the Norse for a few centuries, but what about Scandinavia afterwards? Or Carolingian or modern Germany? What about the Bronze Age? All the tribes were like that. I think it is OK to take a few stereotypical aspects of some human culture and portray a certain tribe that way, but more work should have been done in building the legend and identity of how their tribal totem affected the development of their adopted Garou children.<br /> <br /> I also liked the fact that initially the game included people all over the world where wolves were indigenous, and that certain tribes were associated with certain people, while some tribes were pretty much open and included people of whatever descent. There was an emphasis on seeing things from a Western perspective, but that's OK. People could develop things on their own. I just think that when it came to developing the Uktena and Wendigo, the authors failed to make a distinction between actual Native American culture for people versus an alien tribal culture of werewolves who worship Uktena (which is actually a combination of Uktena and Mishipeshu in the game) and Wendigo. (And to a lesser degree, failed to think who are all the werewolves in eastern Asia - I really hated how this was neglected originally in the tribebooks and how it was made worse by the various KotE/Hengeyokai books in a desperate attempt to create another moneymaking game line). However, I just ignored that and used my own modified house setting.<br /> <br /> Everything that I hear about the fifth edition game books don't make me interested in them. I'm not really interested in how other people are continuing with metaplot. Metaplot kills game lines. They get a narrower and narrower group of people to buy more and more books, while driving away more people from the game entirely. At some point, the cannibalization causes more harm to the bottomline because the pitiful remnant can no longer buy enough additional game books to make up for the attrition.<br /> <br /> I don't mind the idea of Metaplot as separate ideas of how chronicles can become. That gives an ST a toolkit to use - they can take whatever elements they want, ignore it entirely, or use it as the sole basis for a campaign. And if they want to continue with it great. But if not, then next year there is a new Metaplot chronicle guide. But the one can entirely contradict the other because neither is &quot;canon&quot;. They just originate from the original corebook. I approach the different WoD eras as their own thing. 1st/2nd is its own thing, and Revised is its own thing. And my personal chronicle canon is based more on 1st/2nd, ignores Revised completely, and has lots of my own ideas.<br /> <br /> The more time goes by, the more professional supplements look, but in terms of content appear more like fan fiction - a pale imitation of the original taken into whatever weird way the fanboy/girl wanted.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3046-black-fox","name":"Black Fox","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3046_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4187"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T17:53:37-08:00","id":1281413,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1281369#post1281369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and the same goes for their terrible plans for M5.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have a link to Paradox's plans for M5?<br /> <br /> Thanks.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-17T21:25:38-08:00","id":1281446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1281405#post1281405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> A problem with all the tribes to an extent was how much they were derived from specific human ethnic groups/cultures as opposed to being their own thing separate from the culture of their kinfolk. That never made sense for metis and lupus, but even among homids not all homid members came from those cultures. Vikings were specific to the Norse for a few centuries, but what about Scandinavia afterwards? Or Carolingian or modern Germany? What about the Bronze Age? All the tribes were like that. I think it is OK to take a few stereotypical aspects of some human culture and portray a certain tribe that way, but more work should have been done in building the legend and identity of how their tribal totem affected the development of their adopted Garou children.<br /> <br /> I also liked the fact that initially the game included people all over the world where wolves were indigenous, and that certain tribes were associated with certain people, while some tribes were pretty much open and included people of whatever descent. There was an emphasis on seeing things from a Western perspective, but that's OK. People could develop things on their own. I just think that when it came to developing the Uktena and Wendigo, the authors failed to make a distinction between actual Native American culture for people versus an alien tribal culture of werewolves who worship Uktena (which is actually a combination of Uktena and Mishipeshu in the game) and Wendigo. (And to a lesser degree, failed to think who are all the werewolves in eastern Asia - I really hated how this was neglected originally in the tribebooks and how it was made worse by the various KotE/Hengeyokai books in a desperate attempt to create another moneymaking game line). However, I just ignored that and used my own modified house setting.<br /> <br /> Everything that I hear about the fifth edition game books don't make me interested in them. I'm not really interested in how other people are continuing with metaplot. Metaplot kills game lines. They get a narrower and narrower group of people to buy more and more books, while driving away more people from the game entirely. At some point, the cannibalization causes more harm to the bottomline because the pitiful remnant can no longer buy enough additional game books to make up for the attrition.<br /> <br /> I don't mind the idea of Metaplot as separate ideas of how chronicles can become. That gives an ST a toolkit to use - they can take whatever elements they want, ignore it entirely, or use it as the sole basis for a campaign. And if they want to continue with it great. But if not, then next year there is a new Metaplot chronicle guide. But the one can entirely contradict the other because neither is &quot;canon&quot;. They just originate from the original corebook. I approach the different WoD eras as their own thing. 1st/2nd is its own thing, and Revised is its own thing. And my personal chronicle canon is based more on 1st/2nd, ignores Revised completely, and has lots of my own ideas.<br /> <br /> The more time goes by, the more professional supplements look, but in terms of content appear more like fan fiction - a pale imitation of the original taken into whatever weird way the fanboy/girl wanted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Definitely. I didn't want to imply that the faults were just with the Wendigo and Uktena. Like you said, the Germanic cultures the Get took as their primary human kin were much more than the Viking era. And you really hit the nail on the head bringing up how the Lupus and Metis would not be as influenced by these Homid cultures, and how the Wendigo and Uktena need to be Werewolves that lived surrounded by Native peoples and not literally Native peoples. I can say that my ancestors up to today would not want to be around people associated with such beings. They wouldn't be seen as evil, but strongly associated with aspects of existence not to trifled with outside of the times they are required. And yes, Asia has been painfully neglected. Sadly, it wouldn't take more than a few adjustments to the existing material IMO to fix it. Your focus on totems, and really getting deep into their symbolism and folklore is the best route to go IMO too, and possibly how the homid cultures view wolves in the spiritual/mythical sense to finally distinguish what the Garou would be like.<br /> <br /> After reading the 20th editions, I do prefer the games without a metaplot. There's so much more potential and life in the 20th editions than earlier ones. Exploring different metaplots would be preferable, and probably lead to longer lasting game lines.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1281413#post1281413\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you have a link to Paradox's plans for M5?<br /> <br /> Thanks.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be honest, I might have just read about it on other forums. What I heard was the Technocracy was going back to become stand-ins for the Republicans and other right wing parties in the West by encouraging anti-immigrant sentiments because 3rd world people could pose a threat to their paradigm, while the Traditions become magickal versions of ISIS. If true, I guess they've decided the edgy thing would be to make them into what the other stereotypes the other as. Doesn't sound like a good time to me. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T06:08:04-08:00","id":1281496,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, I might have just read about it on other forums. What I heard was the Technocracy was going back to become stand-ins for the Republicans and other right wing parties in the West by encouraging anti-immigrant sentiments because 3rd world people could pose a threat to their paradigm, while the Traditions become magickal versions of ISIS. If true, I guess they've decided the edgy thing would be to make them into what the other stereotypes the other as. Doesn't sound like a good time to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>If my memory serves, that stuff was presented as part of the &quot;One World of Darkness&quot; idea that WW tossed a year or two ago. <br /> <br /> That project didn't made too far as far as I know. Other rumors of that time period haven't been canonized, like Technocracy being behind SI. The ideas presented at that time for M5 (if it happens at all) may change too. Especially now that WW's V5 had such a heavy backlash, I think a change of direction may be in the future.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-18T18:08:20-08:00","id":1281597,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1281446#post1281446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be honest, I might have just read about it on other forums. What I heard was the Technocracy was going back to become stand-ins for the Republicans and other right wing parties in the West by encouraging anti-immigrant sentiments because 3rd world people could pose a threat to their paradigm, while the Traditions become magickal versions of ISIS. If true, I guess they've decided the edgy thing would be to make them into what the other stereotypes the other as. Doesn't sound like a good time to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Lmao.<br /> <br /> I can say with 100% certainty, this is NOT going to happen with M5.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#333333\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">&quot;Steel isn't strong, boy. Flesh is stronger.&quot;</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/95-fat-larry","name":"Fat Larry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar95_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-19T09:24:22-08:00","id":1281650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1281446#post1281446\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">After reading the 20th editions, I do prefer the games without a metaplot. There's so much more potential and life in the 20th editions than earlier ones. Exploring different metaplots would be preferable, and probably lead to longer lasting game lines.</div> </div> </div> </div>W20 has a metaplot, though, and the point in funding it was never to break free from the old story - just to make a deluxe manual as a tribute to the game; all the story from the Impergium to the modern days and the relationships between tribes is all part of the metaplot and an update from how we left the story back in Revised.<br /> <br /> If you aim to no metaplots you should consider the CoD; every game in the new WoD was created to make it local and free from all the binds that came with global scale wars or age-old feuds. Personally I like the cwod story more, even if the nwod uses a better game system.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Everything that I hear about the fifth edition game books don't make me interested in them. I'm not really interested in how other people are continuing with metaplot </div> </div> </div>I'm more interested in how they're going to fix the game mechanics. Werewolf combat is long, clunky and requires a ton of dice since you may end up rolling over 14 of them. And should you end up rolling14 dice of damage, RnG might still give you only 4 successes, easily soaked by a constitution just half of your damage value.<br /> <br /> Therefore, I'll glady embrace any statistical fix or time-saving mechanic the new edition is going to offer, since I can't just apply the V5 system while keeping the same W20 gifts - it just would not work and I don't have the time to rewrite and playtest everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-19T10:32:52-08:00","id":1281658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Fat Larry</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1281597#post1281597\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Lmao.<br /> <br /> I can say with 100% certainty, this is NOT going to happen with M5.</div> </div> </div> </div>After what happened with V5 I'm a 100% certain too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1281650#post1281650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> W20 has a metaplot, though, and the point in funding it was never to break free from the old story - just to make a deluxe manual as a tribute to the game; all the story from the Impergium to the modern days and the relationships between tribes is all part of the metaplot and an update from how we left the story back in Revised.<br /> <br /> If you aim to no metaplots you should consider the CoD; every game in the new WoD was created to make it local and free from all the binds that came with global scale wars or age-old feuds. Personally I like the cwod story more, even if the nwod uses a better game system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was speaking of metaplot in the WoD overall. Some gamelines are sufficated by it more than others. Like I enjoyed the way M20 gave tons of options, because Revised strangled you toward a few styles of play. While most of Werewolves' changes over the years came off more like emphisizing on different aspects of the setting over others or reforms of bad earlier decisions (like Fianna being all up in the Northern Ireland conflict, the Get being down with Neo-Nazis, the Uktena being Werewolf like Tremre/Hermetics instead of defenders of animist and indigenous cultures on a global scale, etc). Like I could care less about Albrecht becoming the Silver Fang king, cause usually that didn't effect our game and we actually liked him as a setting character. <br /> <br /> To me a lot of these things are examples of a rich setting, not metaplot. CoD barely had even a setting for most of their games. With some immagination, you could make up your own, but it felt really pale in comparrison to the global scope of the OWoD. Its why we could never really get into it other than mining it to fill in the holes or give interesting twists to the old games. <br /> <br /> We also didn't care for CoD's mechanics. We took a few things from that for our homebrew rules, but it was another thing that discouraged us from investing in them (we were also largely poor hood kids, and we could buy all the old books super cheep at used book stores). After lurking around gaming forums and seeing what people complain about, mechanics can be almost as subjective as hiw you feel about the fluff. There's so many things my group loved or disliked that other players found the opposite of.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-19T14:34:22-08:00","id":1281695,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1281650#post1281650\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Therefore, I'll glady embrace any statistical fix or time-saving mechanic the new edition is going to offer,....</div> </div> </div> </div>The issue here specifically is if the cure is worse than the disease.<br /> <br /> WtA needs a major system revamp. But V5's mechanics do not offer a solid chassis for a more combat system using playstyle. &quot;Only three rounds of combat then end it&quot; isn't exactly going to be a big hit for people looking for some epic Wyrm fighting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-19T16:26:58-08:00","id":1281713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1281695#post1281695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The issue here specifically is if the cure is worse than the disease.<br /> <br /> WtA needs a major system revamp. But V5's mechanics do not offer a solid chassis for a more combat system using playstyle. &amp;quot;Only three rounds of combat then end it&amp;quot; isn't exactly going to be a big hit for people looking for some epic Wyrm fighting.</div> </div> </div> </div>What about adopting thr Storypath system? I haven't read it directly, but I've heard nothing but praise so far.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T02:57:11-08:00","id":1281762,"title":"","content":"I would love to see the cWoD games done in the Storypath system, even if it's not clear how that would ever happen outside of a fan project.<br /> <br /> The combat systems in general feel faster and robust even if combat can take awhile. Combat rounds go quicker, and there's some neat things it uses to accomplish that (for example, while your roll Defense, you only roll Defense once the first time you're attacked in the round and it stands for the rest of the round rather than rolling per attack), but it also adds some nice tactical depth (such as when you make your Defense roll, you can choose to spend successes on things besides how hard it is for attackers to hit you so there's a choice to make there) which is fun for people that like it but might be a bit too much for others. Storypath characters also tend to be pretty tough to it can take a while to actually beat a character. Which is good for a pack of werewolves facing off against a single opponent so the NPC doesn't go down instantly, but can also get a bit to be a bit of a slog until players get a hang of the Stunt system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T18:00:08-08:00","id":1281851,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1281762#post1281762\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would love to see the cWoD games done in the Storypath system, even if it's not clear how that would ever happen outside of a fan project.<br /> <br /> The combat systems in general feel faster and robust even if combat can take awhile. Combat rounds go quicker, and there's some neat things it uses to accomplish that (for example, while your roll Defense, you only roll Defense once the first time you're attacked in the round and it stands for the rest of the round rather than rolling per attack), but it also adds some nice tactical depth (such as when you make your Defense roll, you can choose to spend successes on things besides how hard it is for attackers to hit you so there's a choice to make there) which is fun for people that like it but might be a bit too much for others. Storypath characters also tend to be pretty tough to it can take a while to actually beat a character. Which is good for a pack of werewolves facing off against a single opponent so the NPC doesn't go down instantly, but can also get a bit to be a bit of a slog until players get a hang of the Stunt system.</div> </div> </div> </div>I might have to buy Scion or Trinity to have a look at its nuts and bolts then.<br /> <br /> I wouldn't claim to be any sort of expert on game engine design, but my group did cobble together this abomination of a system over the years. We had lots of fun using a modified mix of Exalted 2E's tick system and WoD Comabt for one example.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T22:41:40-08:00","id":1281878,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1281695#post1281695\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;Only three rounds of combat then end it&quot; isn't exactly going to be a big hit for people looking for some epic Wyrm fighting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, that part was horrible and paragon of lazy game design. I was mostly speaking though of the &quot;brawl roll vs brawl roll, hurt the loser with the difference&quot;. It concentrates attack, damage, dodge and soak roll in a single contested action. But even something more Exalted-like, where you don't roll damage but just subtract your soak total from STR, would cut some needless roll from the game; but Exalted is a different game, with perfect defenses and 20 hp for character, you'd have to tune it carefully to set the lethality just right.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> CoD barely had even a setting for most of their games. With some immagination, you could make up your own, but it felt really pale in comparrison to the global scope of the OWoD. Its why we could never really get into it other than mining it to fill in the holes or give interesting twists to the old games. </div> </div> </div>The main issue with the CWOD was having global superstructures controlling everything. So, Vampire players always had some Elder League over them ready to rain hell if they happened to do big things, young mages had insanely powerful immortal archmages controlling everything from the Umbra, Werewolves had global Pentex conspirations and an epic fight for the end of times... CoD just made it smaller, freeing the storytellers from the burdens of a setting that yes, gave you tools but bound you at the same times.<br /> <br /> I.e: Camarilla and Sabbat are obvious rivals in Masquerade, the Tzimisce are almost nonexistent in the Camarilla; in Requiem, though, the clans are not so structured and the covenants have fluid relationships - Lancea sanctum and Invictus can coexist peacefully in a town, but also be at war should the ST want it.<br /> <br /> Also, Mage Revised might have been a bit more contained in power level, but had the target of putting the player characters as absolute protagonists of the campaign: the Archmages are lost, the spirit world hard to reach, the ancient Chantries destroyed in the war... everything left were a bunch of half-trained newbies and a setting where the strongest mages had Arete 4. Sure, no more spaceships bombarding the gates of Doissetep but through cutting the Ascension war the game went back to the Ascension quest. So yes, I frowned for the loss of the Umbra at first but after a while I could actually appreciate the direction the game was taking, and I believe I like Revised more than all the other versions now - including M20.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T23:31:29-08:00","id":1281889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1281851#post1281851\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I might have to buy Scion or Trinity to have a look at its nuts and bolts then.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a Storypath preview document that covers a lot of the base rules. The different core books are really more important if you want to see how they adjust things for the different games to stress different aspects; especially if you were interested in hacking a Storypath WOD. Like Scion 2e tends to down play the importance of equipment to focus on the mythological side of things, while Trinity 2e has more tech in it to allow the sci-fi side of the setting to shine. You see this more in the expansion cores (Hero and Aeon) over the initial cores (Origin and Continuum) which tend to be closer in material.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I wouldn't claim to be any sort of expert on game engine design, but my group did cobble together this abomination of a system over the years. </div> </div> </div>The hardest part is the powers really. Storypath works on a very different concept of how to implement powers than the WoD/CofD, Exalted or even Trinity and Scion 1e.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1281878#post1281878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, that part was horrible and paragon of lazy game design.</div> </div> </div> </div>But exactly what I'm not confident in the V5 and BNS WtA books leading to a fun combat system for W5 even if some fixes that should happen get done.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I was mostly speaking though of the &quot;brawl roll vs brawl roll, hurt the loser with the difference&quot;. </div> </div> </div>Even this is a problem though. It works well enough for people that are generally on par with each other and roughly equal numbers of people on both side of the fight.<br /> <br /> A bunch of Garou vs. a big dangerous bane is insanely hard to avoid either being a complete let down, or a TPK. Yes it compresses the systems. but you lose the ability to have variety in combat that doesn't quickly sway to one sided.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T13:54:05-08:00","id":1282006,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1281878#post1281878\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The main issue with the CWOD was having global superstructures controlling everything. So, Vampire players always had some Elder League over them ready to rain hell if they happened to do big things, young mages had insanely powerful immortal archmages controlling everything from the Umbra, Werewolves had global Pentex conspirations and an epic fight for the end of times... CoD just made it smaller, freeing the storytellers from the burdens of a setting that yes, gave you tools but bound you at the same times.<br /> <br /> I.e: Camarilla and Sabbat are obvious rivals in Masquerade, the Tzimisce are almost nonexistent in the Camarilla; in Requiem, though, the clans are not so structured and the covenants have fluid relationships - Lancea sanctum and Invictus can coexist peacefully in a town, but also be at war should the ST want it.<br /> <br /> Also, Mage Revised might have been a bit more contained in power level, but had the target of putting the player characters as absolute protagonists of the campaign: the Archmages are lost, the spirit world hard to reach, the ancient Chantries destroyed in the war... everything left were a bunch of half-trained newbies and a setting where the strongest mages had Arete 4. Sure, no more spaceships bombarding the gates of Doissetep but through cutting the Ascension war the game went back to the Ascension quest. So yes, I frowned for the loss of the Umbra at first but after a while I could actually appreciate the direction the game was taking, and I believe I like Revised more than all the other versions now - including M20.</div> </div> </div> </div>We never felt restricted by the existence of elders of any kind or the larger factions and shadow nations among the supernaturals. The questions of why didn't King Albrect, Porthos, Leigh, one of the Death Lords, or Lucita not drop in to save the day instead of our player group never factored into the equation of our games. They only existed in so far as was needed for our stories. World building can be fun, but sometimes you want a setting ready to play in or at least serve as an example. Besides, to me at least, individual septs, vampire societies within individual cities, or chantries/contructs seemed independent enough in their canon set-up for their allegience to larger factions not to be an issue either. Overall, people should like what they like. It's just, taken as a whole, most of my friends didn't find CoD as engaging or compelling as a setting when compared to the CWoD. It doesn't mean that one game line is inferior to the other. <br /> <br /> What I did like about most of the 20th editions, is they felt like the 1st/2nd edition books with less cumbersome metaplot additions. It all felt very open and optional for any of that, especially since it's been over a decade for most of the games to have any material released. It made me realize I don't really care to see what all these NPCs have been doing or what plots are still relevant, especially since this would have to be, for lack of a better term, a alternate timeline since their world ended back in 2004. Preferably I would like any 5th edition to be released with a new slate. I would like them to be updated a bit to clear off the 90s dust, and then propelled forward with new plots and characters.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21481-onkwe","name":"Onkwe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar21481_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"162"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T15:16:52-08:00","id":1282022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Onkwe</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1282006#post1282006\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We never felt restricted by the existence of elders of any kind or the larger factions and shadow nations among the supernaturals. The questions of why didn't King Albrect, Porthos, Leigh, one of the Death Lords, or Lucita not drop in to save the day instead of our player group never factored into the equation of our games. They only existed in so far as was needed for our stories. World building can be fun, but sometimes you want a setting ready to play in or at least serve as an example. Besides, to me at least, individual septs, vampire societies within individual cities, or chantries/contructs seemed independent enough in their canon set-up for their allegience to larger factions not to be an issue either. Overall, people should like what they like. It's just, taken as a whole, most of my friends didn't find CoD as engaging or compelling as a setting when compared to the CWoD. It doesn't mean that one game line is inferior to the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>I personally think that having the institutions and &quot;superstructures&quot; existing is a benefit to the roleplaying options of a game.<br /> Firstly, it imposes the gothic punk feel, it's hard to rebel against the tyranny of the system when the &quot;system&quot; is a couple of guys above you. It's also too easy to see the fallibility of individuals and empathize with their hard decisions when you can personally know them. When the people at the top are so far above you, it gives more of a menacing feeling from the unknown.<br /> The games never needed to explore that aspect in depth of course.<br /> But with CoD Vampires, you can too easily get in to the powerful elite, become prince, since they don't have the weight of a bureaucracy to back them against plays. There isn't the follow up since most cities are more independent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T00:34:19-08:00","id":1282807,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Black Fox</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1281405#post1281405\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The more time goes by, the more professional supplements look, but in terms of content appear more like fan fiction - a pale imitation of the original taken into whatever weird way the fanboy/girl wanted.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This last line was unnecessary to an otherwise valid post and is at the very least insulting to the writers who have worked for both WW and OPP, which is a rules violation. I'm issuing a warning not to post comments like this again in the future, please and thank you.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> <span style=\"font-family:georgia\"><span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Onyx Path Forum Administrator</b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b><span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\">Posts in this color are moderator posts</span></b></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:comic sans ms\"><span style=\"color:#00FF00\">Posts in this color mean a Great Old One has driven me mad.</span></span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11-darksider","name":"Darksider","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11_2.jpeg","title":"Forum Administrator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1692"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T23:07:40-08:00","id":1282969,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1282022#post1282022\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I personally think that having the institutions and &quot;superstructures&quot; existing is a benefit to the roleplaying options of a game.<br /> Firstly, it imposes the gothic punk feel, it's hard to rebel against the tyranny of the system when the &quot;system&quot; is a couple of guys above you. It's also too easy to see the fallibility of individuals and empathize with their hard decisions when you can personally know them. When the people at the top are so far above you, it gives more of a menacing feeling from the unknown.<br /> The games never needed to explore that aspect in depth of course.<br /> But with CoD Vampires, you can too easily get in to the powerful elite, become prince, since they don't have the weight of a bureaucracy to back them against plays. There isn't the follow up since most cities are more independent.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> CoD games are explicitly NOT punk? I mean not every interpretation of modern horror has to have punk baked into it and I think that's a solid defining difference between the two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T04:11:32-08:00","id":1283016,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darksider</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1282807#post1282807\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This last line was unnecessary to an otherwise valid post and is at the very least insulting to the writers who have worked for both WW and OPP, which is a rules violation. I'm issuing a warning not to post comments like this again in the future, please and thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>If critique is a a rule violation then some rule has to change.<br /> He believes that the books lack professionality, good, it's an opinion like any others. Feel free to defend the authors but censorship is disproportionate.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We never felt restricted by the existence of elders of any kind or the larger factions and shadow nations among the supernaturals. The questions of why didn't King Albrect, Porthos, Leigh, one of the Death Lords, or Lucita not drop in to save the day instead of our player group never factored into the equation of our games. They only existed in so far as was needed for our stories </div> </div> </div>The point is not having Etrius come to New Hope, Pennsylvania, to spank the neonate PC that insulted a local Tremere, but knowing that if you violate the local Camarilla you'll be hunted in the whole world by the Archons. It's a social power much different from the VtR one, where if you violate the rules of the local Prince you can safely find haven in every other city.<br /> <br /> And to be clear, I like the metaplot and how it evolved in the years (save some exception, like, how the hell did Theo Bell manage to kill Vitel, it makes no sense); but people who disliked it found their haven in the products of the new Chronicle of Darkness.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T12:13:31-08:00","id":1283090,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1283016#post1283016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If critique is a a rule violation then some rule has to change.</div> </div> </div> </div>Calling the supplement developers and authors fanboys/girls isn't a critique.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The point is not having Etrius come to New Hope, Pennsylvania, to spank the neonate PC that insulted a local Tremere, but knowing that if you violate the local Camarilla you'll be hunted in the whole world by the Archons. </div> </div> </div>Eh? I think for most WoD fans the point is far more the depth of the setting than the implications of the setting. High level NPCs aren't really there to cement specific realities on the setting; pissing off your local Sept doesn't mean Albercht is going send people to investigate. They're there to flush out the setting because it's designed as a top heavy setting where not knowing who holds positions doesn't make a lot of sense.<br /> <br /> Some people would argue this is a punk thing, though I do challenge the idea that punk aesthetics are so limited.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's a social power much different from the VtR one, where if you violate the rules of the local Prince you can safely find haven in every other city. </div> </div> </div>Maybe, maybe not. The locals you're intruding on might not like you showing up; unlike VtM you can be killed on the spot for trying to settle in a new city without permission because you don't have a Camarilla to rely on to keep certain levels of mutual dealing intact. Fleeing to a new city in VtR is a big enough risk that despite how different social power is handled... the result for player characters is largely the same: respect the Prince's power because the alternatives are usually worse.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And to be clear, I like the metaplot and how it evolved in the years (save some exception, like, how the hell did Theo Bell manage to kill Vitel, it makes no sense); but people who disliked it found their haven in the products of the new Chronicle of Darkness. </div> </div> </div>This is a bit of a false dichotomy. CofD vs. WoD is a lot more than metaplot vs. not, and plenty of people might like the WoD more despite the metaplot and would rather the metaplot be handled more like how Exalted or the 20th books do (that is, focus on backstory and where the metaplot might go, than on advancing the metaplot with new books) treats the setting. This is especially true of fans heavily invested in the existing lore, because metaplot shakeups around new editions tend to be the most disruptive.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T13:47:57-08:00","id":1283111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maris Streck</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1283016#post1283016\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If critique is a a rule violation then some rule has to change. He believes that the books lack professionality, good, it's an opinion like any others. Feel free to defend the authors but censorship is disproportionate.</div> </div> </div> </div> <span style=\"color:red\">Critique is not a rule violation, but disrespect is. A disrespectful comment is not exempted from the rules simply because it is also critical. The rules also state that if you take issue with a moderator\u2019s action, to use the contact us link rather than disputing it publicly.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T19:00:46-08:00","id":1283164,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1283090#post1283090\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Calling the supplement developers and authors fanboys/girls isn't a critique.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is that an insult on these forums? =P I thought we all were fanboys/fangirls.<br /> The way I took it he was simply complaining on the lack of coherence between supplements.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Eh? I think for most WoD fans the point is far more the depth of the setting than the implications of the setting. High level NPCs aren't really there to cement specific realities on the setting; pissing off your local Sept doesn't mean Albercht is going send people to investigate. </div> </div> </div>I think that Werewolf is less invasive than Vampire in this sense, since the Garou society is really fractured. But yes, my point was that so much background ends up binding you, apologies if I expressed it poorly. Not that you can't make your own personal campaign putting the Lasombra in the Camarilla and the Tremere in the Sabbat, but many players will complain if the setting is not respected and you certainly can't modify it to such an extent in open events (i.e. public RP tournaments must be respectful of the setting or they'll miss the point).<br /> <br /> Aka life is easier if the game is more how you like it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This is a bit of a false dichotomy. CofD vs. WoD is a lot more than metaplot vs. not, and plenty of people might like the WoD more despite the metaplot and would rather the metaplot be handled more like how Exalted or the 20th books do (that is, focus on backstory and where the metaplot might go, than on advancing the metaplot with new books) treats the setting. This is especially true of fans heavily invested in the existing lore, because metaplot shakeups around new editions tend to be the most disruptive. </div> </div> </div>I was simply considrering the games from the metaplot viewpoint, didn't mean to imply there were no other differences between the IPs.<br /> And I totally understand your meaning. A lot of people took it badly when they removed the Tremere Antitribu or when the Avatar storm refocused Mage on the mundane world; on the very topic of V5 there were a lot of people unsatisfied with the second inquisition, too. I must say, though, that in the WtA setting very little changed between versions... maybe just the Stargazers position in the Garou nation but I can't recall any significative update on the metaplot in the years. What did we have, the crowning of Albrecht and the Skinner adventure serie?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13673-maris-streck","name":"Maris Streck","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13673_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"420"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T21:31:49-08:00","id":1283187,"title":"","content":"WtA had a lot of metaplot changes over the years, but WtA generally avoided messing with the base formula (at least until BNS WtA) No Tribes changing allegiances (yes the Stargazers did in Revised, but W20 undid that, and the smallest Tribe leaving was a blip), or being nearly wiped out, or things of that nature. Septs fell, NPCs died, whole groups of antagonists like the Seventh Generation were destroyed, etc.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-28T17:17:00-08:00","id":1283392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1282969#post1282969\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">CoD games are explicitly NOT punk? I mean not every interpretation of modern horror has to have punk baked into it and I think that's a solid defining difference between the two.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not quite sure of your message, since I'm a fan of full sentences to the point of being overly verbose to make sure that I have left myself clear!<br /> <br /> I Assume (correct me if I'm wrong) that you think I'm saying Requiem is not punk?<br /> I think they have less punk aspects because you can get out the the trap of being the oppressed more easily than in Masquerade. In Masquerade, being a Prince, Archon or even Justicar and you are still oppressed by the inner council. Hell; even the inner Council would likely have pressure from the elders behind the creation of the Camarilla, up to the Clan founders.<br /> I'm not saying that it's not punk...<br /> On the flip side; I'm not saying that Requiem is punk; I agree that gothic can be without punk: Otherwise it'd be advertised as &quot;Gothic&quot; instead of &quot;Gothic Punk&quot; since punk aspects would be implied by the use of &quot;Gothic&quot; automatically.<br /> <br /> What I'm saying is 1) I believe that the superstructures as discussed are a benefit to roleplaying because they give multilayered political roleplaying opportunities; getting to the top of a city is not the end of that roleplaying experience with peers and superiors, because you will always have peers and superiors.<br /> 2) I don't actually care what Requiem/Forseaken etc is any more. It doesn't meet my needs, or the needs of those I play with; either in mechanics or themes; I'm completely talking about the WORLD of darkness instead of Chronicles of Darkness; as per the sorting of the forum.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T03:01:34-08:00","id":1283475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1283111#post1283111\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <span style=\"color:red\">Critique is not a rule violation, but disrespect is. A disrespectful comment is not exempted from the rules simply because it is also critical. The rules also state that if you take issue with a moderator\u2019s action, to use the contact us link rather than disputing it publicly.</span></div> </div> </div> </div>Well, I too feel, on occasion, that newer books published by OPP and BNS are written in ways that I would describe as &quot;fanboy/fangirl&quot;-like. This might be the case, it might be attributed to an (for me) unsatisfactory editing process or other factors I can't imagine. Thing is, it is an impression I have, too.<br /> <br /> Your point is, that you assume that &quot;as if written by a fanboy/fangirl&quot; is disrespectful. Well, this could be argued. One might find certain characteristics in the works of fans who contribute to a shared universe, one would not find in work of people who aren't that invested. Whether or not that is a good or a bat thing is also up to personal taste. In any case, I don't see &quot;fanboy/fangirl&quot;-like as a disrespectful statement in and of its own.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich","name":"heinrich","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1008_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1802"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-29T20:57:52-08:00","id":1283645,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1008-heinrich\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1008_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1008\" data-vbnamecard=\"1008\">heinrich</a> <br /> There's also the other rule about questioning the mod's judgement in private instead of public. Even if you're right on the above, I'd suggest following that one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T07:31:01-08:00","id":1283714,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>heinrich</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-on-future-werewolf-5ed-by-looking-at-the-bns-book?p=1283475#post1283475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I too feel, on occasion, that newer books published by OPP and BNS are written in ways that I would describe as &amp;quot;fanboy/fangirl&amp;quot;-like. This might be the case, it might be attributed to an (for me) unsatisfactory editing process or other factors I can't imagine. Thing is, it is an impression I have, too.<br /> <br /> Your point is, that you assume that &amp;quot;as if written by a fanboy/fangirl&amp;quot; is disrespectful. Well, this could be argued. One might find certain characteristics in the works of fans who contribute to a shared universe, one would not find in work of people who aren't that invested. Whether or not that is a good or a bat thing is also up to personal taste. In any case, I don't see &amp;quot;fanboy/fangirl&amp;quot;-like as a disrespectful statement in and of its own.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">What did I JUST SAY about using the Contact Us link?</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-30T15:24:06-08:00","id":1283808,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1055797-thoughts-o